512
00:17:36.970 --> 00:17:38.840
And so, when I did,

513
00:17:38.840 --> 00:17:39.673
I said I'm just gonna kind of

514
00:17:39.673 --> 00:17:41.650
be the most chill vegetarian I can be.

515
00:17:41.650 --> 00:17:43.290
I'm not gonna tell anyone they should do this.

516
00:17:43.290 --> 00:17:44.967
I'm just gonna say, "Hey, it's working for me.

517
00:17:44.967 --> 00:17:47.630
"If you wanna try it, here are some tools."

518
00:17:47.630 --> 00:17:49.150
So, Seth Godin has that exact same approach

519
00:17:49.150 --> 00:17:50.440
to me to marketing,

520
00:17:50.440 --> 00:17:52.350
where it doesn't feel like you're being sold.

521
00:17:52.350 --> 00:17:53.610
It just feels like someone's

522
00:17:53.610 --> 00:17:56.221
a lot of fun to listen to and learn from.

523
00:17:56.221 --> 00:17:59.300
So, I think my vibe very much resonated with his

524
00:17:59.300 --> 00:18:02.630
and he announced that he was gonna have 15 readers

525
00:18:02.630 --> 00:18:05.460
come spend a week in his office and work on projects

526
00:18:06.380 --> 00:18:08.276
and I applied and I figured

527
00:18:08.276 --> 00:18:09.190
I'm not actually gonna get this,

528
00:18:09.190 --> 00:18:10.410
but I did a little video

529
00:18:10.410 --> 00:18:12.740
and he had written the blurb for my first book.

530
00:18:12.740 --> 00:18:14.720
He'd written a nice little thing

531
00:18:14.720 --> 00:18:15.610
because I had heard

532
00:18:15.610 --> 00:18:19.140
he was mostly vegetarian or vegan or something back then.

