So, I think it's finding the foods that you already like

1063
00:36:49.780 --> 00:36:53.230
and then I think there's a necessary understanding

1064
00:36:53.230 --> 00:36:55.900
of calorie density and nutrient density,

1065
00:36:55.900 --> 00:36:57.520
at least as far as getting the most mileage

1066
00:36:57.520 --> 00:36:58.820
from your plant-based diet.

1067
00:36:58.820 --> 00:37:00.720
Yeah, because that's one of the things

1068
00:37:00.720 --> 00:37:02.240
that I hear often.

1069
00:37:02.240 --> 00:37:03.450
I'm sure you do as well.

1070
00:37:03.450 --> 00:37:05.400
I tried this but I was hungry all the time.

1071
00:37:05.400 --> 00:37:07.100
I'm like, you're not eating enough.

1072
00:37:07.100 --> 00:37:09.565
Or frequently enough in many cases.

1073
00:37:09.565 --> 00:37:11.229
Well, can I tell you a scenario?

1074
00:37:11.229 --> 00:37:12.062
Sure.

1075
00:37:12.062 --> 00:37:12.895
So, this is--

1076
00:37:12.895 --> 00:37:13.728
This is what you're here to do, Robert.

1077
00:37:13.728 --> 00:37:14.570
Tell me the scenario.

1078
00:37:14.570 --> 00:37:15.590
So, this is so common.

1079
00:37:15.590 --> 00:37:18.400
I've watched this over the last 25 years

1080
00:37:18.400 --> 00:37:20.700
and people often come to me in conversation or email

1081
00:37:20.700 --> 00:37:21.533
with this topic.

1082
00:37:21.533 --> 00:37:23.680
So, let's say you're a male athlete,

1083
00:37:23.680 --> 00:37:25.440
'cause I interact with a lot of them

1084
00:37:25.440 --> 00:37:27.400
through the bodybuilding sphere.

1085
00:37:27.400 --> 00:37:30.480
So, they're consuming, let's say, 3,000 calories

1086
00:37:30.480 --> 00:37:32.227
on an omnivorous diet, right?

1087
00:37:32.227 --> 00:37:34.600
And they switched to an all plant-based diet

1088
00:37:34.600 --> 00:37:37.500
and now they're down to maybe consuming

1089
00:37:37.500 --> 00:37:39.800
2,000 calories or 2,200 calories.

1090
00:37:39.800 --> 00:37:43.120
And they're like, man, I've lost some weight.

1091
00:37:43.120 --> 00:37:44.390
My energy has gone down.

1092
00:37:44.390 --> 00:37:46.553
I'm not as strong.

1093
00:37:46.553 --> 00:37:49.370
You just cut out a third of your calorie intake

1094
00:37:49.370 --> 00:37:51.770
without being aware of it until now,

1095
00:37:51.770 --> 00:37:53.420
until once we evaluate it.

1096
00:37:53.420 --> 00:37:54.660
And this happens all the time

1097
00:37:54.660 --> 00:37:56.670
because the calorie density

1098
00:37:56.670 --> 00:37:58.970
of meat and animal protein is so high

1099
00:37:58.970 --> 00:38:02.860
and it also comes packaged oftentimes with lots of oil

1100
00:38:02.860 --> 00:38:07.200
and other cheese or dairy products

1101
00:38:07.200 --> 00:38:09.540
or sour cream or whatever, eggs,

1102
00:38:09.540 --> 00:38:13.050
where you're getting a much higher calorie intake.

1103
00:38:13.050 --> 00:38:15.760
And so, if you're a football player, a bodybuilder,

1104
00:38:15.760 --> 00:38:17.990
a weightlifter or a basketball player,

1105
00:38:17.990 --> 00:38:19.880
really active in any kind of sport

1106
00:38:19.880 --> 00:38:23.500
and you significantly reduce your calorie intake

1107
00:38:23.500 --> 00:38:25.180
because you're eating salads

1108
00:38:25.180 --> 00:38:26.300
and fruits and vegetables

1109
00:38:26.300 --> 00:38:28.090
and you're just omitting animal protein

1110
00:38:28.090 --> 00:38:30.340
without an awareness of calorie density,

1111
00:38:30.340 --> 00:38:32.178
of course, you're gonna have lower energy.

1112
00:38:32.178 --> 00:38:33.980
Energy is from our calorie intake.

1113
00:38:33.980 --> 00:38:35.800
Of course, you're gonna lose some weight

1114
00:38:35.800 --> 00:38:39.330
because you can't mathematically maintain that mass

1115
00:38:39.330 --> 00:38:41.490
in a calorie deficit, in reduction

1116
00:38:41.490 --> 00:38:42.900
and that happens all the time.

1117
00:38:42.900 --> 00:38:44.420
Yeah, the thing is,

1118
00:38:44.420 --> 00:38:45.560
is that you don't realize

1119
00:38:45.560 --> 00:38:48.800
that you're running a caloric deficit

1120
00:38:48.800 --> 00:38:50.790
compared to the way that you used to be eating

1121
00:38:50.790 --> 00:38:54.020
because if you amp up the fiber in your diet,

1122
00:38:54.020 --> 00:38:55.260
you get full,

1123
00:38:55.260 --> 00:38:56.270
you'll feel full--

1124
00:38:56.270 --> 00:38:57.410
And it happens all the time.

1125
00:38:57.410 --> 00:38:58.243
And so, you think that you're eating

1126
00:38:58.243 --> 00:38:59.250
as much as you were before

1127
00:38:59.250 --> 00:39:01.030
when in fact you're eating quite a bit less.

1128
00:39:01.030 --> 00:39:02.300
Which is, that's why I said frequently,

1129
00:39:02.300 --> 00:39:04.300
because you think you're gonna try

1130
00:39:04.300 --> 00:39:05.290
to eat a whole lot at a meal

1131
00:39:05.290 --> 00:39:06.600
to make up for the fact

1132
00:39:06.600 --> 00:39:08.500
that your food doesn't have as many calories, but can't.

1133
00:39:08.500 --> 00:39:11.220
You get full and you feel like you've eaten just as much.

1134
00:39:11.220 --> 00:39:12.053
So, the trick for me

1135
00:39:12.053 --> 00:39:14.560
when I'm trying to put weight on or keep weight on

1136
00:39:14.560 --> 00:39:15.900
is just eat more often

1137
00:39:15.900 --> 00:39:17.403
just as much as I can.

1138
00:39:17.403 --> 00:39:20.440
Not at any one meal, but just throughout the day.

1139
00:39:20.440 --> 00:39:24.350
Let's talk about a little bit about the why.

1140
00:39:24.350 --> 00:39:25.840
We probably should've started with this.

1141
00:39:25.840 --> 00:39:28.910
Why is this something that people should be thinking about?

1142
00:39:28.910 --> 00:39:31.070
Why is this a better way to go?

1143
00:39:31.070 --> 00:39:34.060
Weren't we born and bred to be omnivorous?

1144
00:39:34.060 --> 00:39:35.400
What's so terrible

1145
00:39:35.400 --> 00:39:40.400
about eating a moderate and healthy omnivorous diet?

1146
00:39:41.660 --> 00:39:46.130
Yeah, I think a number of things problematic with that.

1147
00:39:46.130 --> 00:39:49.770
One is that that's a diet lifestyle

1148
00:39:49.770 --> 00:39:54.770
that contributes to higher cases mortality across the board.

1149
00:39:54.830 --> 00:39:57.150
A plant-based diet is, as Gregory says,

1150
00:39:57.150 --> 00:40:01.330
it should be the default diet until proven otherwise,

1151
00:40:01.330 --> 00:40:04.580
because it can reduce the risk of all-cause mortality.

1152
00:40:04.580 --> 00:40:06.480
For me, I got into this

1153
00:40:07.530 --> 00:40:11.447
literally having dairy cows as friends, as Pat says.

1154
00:40:11.447 --> 00:40:14.460
How do so many people in the plant-based movement

1155
00:40:14.460 --> 00:40:16.325
are people who grew up on farm?

1156
00:40:16.325 --> 00:40:17.158
(laughs)

1157
00:40:17.158 --> 00:40:18.198
Like Dr. Klaper--

1158
00:40:18.198 --> 00:40:19.253
Well, there's something to that

1159
00:40:19.253 --> 00:40:20.940
because you look at animals differently.

1160
00:40:20.940 --> 00:40:23.160
How you would treat your dogs,

1161
00:40:23.160 --> 00:40:25.180
we just extend that to chickens,

1162
00:40:25.180 --> 00:40:27.160
because think about this, Rich.

1163
00:40:27.160 --> 00:40:28.540
I grew up on a farm where you raised animals

1164
00:40:28.540 --> 00:40:29.570
from when they're babies

1165
00:40:29.570 --> 00:40:31.610
and if they're taken from their mothers,

1166
00:40:31.610 --> 00:40:33.353
who is their new best friend, it's you?

1167
00:40:33.353 --> 00:40:34.740
I used to bottle feed baby calves

1168
00:40:34.740 --> 00:40:36.750
before getting on the school bus.

1169
00:40:36.750 --> 00:40:38.760
I used to hang out with baby chicks

1170
00:40:38.760 --> 00:40:41.630
and play a little elevator game with my hand.

1171
00:40:41.630 --> 00:40:42.610
They trust you.

1172
00:40:42.610 --> 00:40:46.090
You are their person just like for your dog.

1173
00:40:46.090 --> 00:40:48.010
You are that person.

1174
00:40:48.010 --> 00:40:50.670
So, I think for me,

1175
00:40:50.670 --> 00:40:52.530
I just looked at animals differently

1176
00:40:52.530 --> 00:40:54.410
and that was something that

1177
00:40:54.410 --> 00:40:57.250
even if I thought I might have diminished returns

1178
00:40:57.250 --> 00:40:59.410
on athletic success adopting this lifestyle,

1179
00:40:59.410 --> 00:41:00.860
I was willing to do it

1180
00:41:00.860 --> 00:41:03.580
because it just spoke to me.

1181
00:41:03.580 --> 00:41:05.600
And that's what compelled me

1182
00:41:05.600 --> 00:41:07.573
all these years later for 25 years.

1183
00:41:08.648 --> 00:41:11.430
Luckily, it didn't have a hindrance.

1184
00:41:11.430 --> 00:41:12.850
It didn't have any adverse effects

1185
00:41:12.850 --> 00:41:14.010
on my athletic performance.

1186
00:41:14.010 --> 00:41:15.610
In fact, maybe helped it,

1187
00:41:15.610 --> 00:41:17.486
but that's certainly one of the reasons,

1188
00:41:17.486 --> 00:41:21.970
is allowing animals to live lives

1189
00:41:21.970 --> 00:41:23.340
free of fear, pain, and suffering

1190
00:41:23.340 --> 00:41:24.500
and I think that's valid.

1191
00:41:24.500 --> 00:41:26.670
I think that's worth considering.

1192
00:41:26.670 --> 00:41:28.390
We can talk about all the environmental factors

1193
00:41:28.390 --> 00:41:30.240
and I don't even know a lot of those nuances.

1194
00:41:30.240 --> 00:41:31.190
I'm not a scientist.

1195
00:41:31.190 --> 00:41:33.980
I don't understand all the greenhouse gas stuff.

1196
00:41:33.980 --> 00:41:37.570
I see the quotes and how many gallons of water are used

1197
00:41:38.637 --> 00:41:40.830
just to raise animals and all of that.

1198
00:41:40.830 --> 00:41:41.770
Of course, it's important to me,

1199
00:41:41.770 --> 00:41:43.660
but I can't really speak to that necessarily.

1200
00:41:43.660 --> 00:41:48.660
I can speak to my cause or my why

1201
00:41:48.770 --> 00:41:52.678
and I can speak to the fact that so many people,

1202
00:41:52.678 --> 00:41:54.110
even if it's anecdotal,

1203
00:41:54.110 --> 00:41:56.420
the stuff that I've seen for 25 years,

1204
00:41:56.420 --> 00:42:00.720
people who are able to overcome obesity, overcome illnesses,

1205
00:42:00.720 --> 00:42:02.690
become the best versions of themselves,

1206
00:42:02.690 --> 00:42:04.810
feel better than they've ever felt in their lives

1207
00:42:04.810 --> 00:42:07.010
because of a plant-based diet.

1208
00:42:07.010 --> 00:42:09.400
And I've also seen how people, including my family,

1209
00:42:09.400 --> 00:42:11.100
'cause both sides of my family

1210
00:42:11.100 --> 00:42:12.820
come from farming backgrounds, both parents.

1211
00:42:12.820 --> 00:42:14.500
So, my aunts, and uncles are all farmers.

1212
00:42:14.500 --> 00:42:16.901
They still own lots of acres and they farm

1213
00:42:16.901 --> 00:42:19.740
and they have the health problems

1214
00:42:19.740 --> 00:42:22.430
that Klaper and others

1215
00:42:22.430 --> 00:42:26.130
who are the same age bracket or older don't have.

1216
00:42:26.130 --> 00:42:27.410
And again, those are just examples,

1217
00:42:27.410 --> 00:42:29.630
but they're close to home.

1218
00:42:29.630 --> 00:42:34.630
I lost multiple relatives recently to diet related diseases

1219
00:42:35.140 --> 00:42:38.010
and that does hit close to home.

1220
00:42:38.010 --> 00:42:40.990
And I know that a plant-based diet can help with that

1221
00:42:40.990 --> 00:42:42.510
because of Forks Over Knives

1222
00:42:42.510 --> 00:42:45.490
and Campbell and Esselstyn and Barnard and Klaper

1223
00:42:45.490 --> 00:42:48.980
and all those, Ornish, the legends in this game.

1224
00:42:48.980 --> 00:42:50.220
And I think for people listening,

1225
00:42:50.220 --> 00:42:51.860
it's worth giving it a shot

1226
00:42:51.860 --> 00:42:56.070
because the fear of, for me, at least,

1227
00:42:56.070 --> 00:42:58.500
and I know you've experienced a little bit of this

1228
00:42:58.500 --> 00:42:59.430
in part of your journey.

1229
00:42:59.430 --> 00:43:02.220
The fear of something like a heart attack

1230
00:43:02.220 --> 00:43:05.193
or a diet related disease that sneaks up on me,

1231
00:43:05.193 --> 00:43:06.540
that's kind of scary to me.

1232
00:43:06.540 --> 00:43:08.230
And if I can reduce the risk of that

1233
00:43:08.230 --> 00:43:11.010
and live a long, healthy life,

1234
00:43:11.010 --> 00:43:12.770
that's worth it for me.

1235
00:43:12.770 --> 00:43:14.430
And still kill it in the weight room.

1236
00:43:14.430 --> 00:43:15.524
Yeah.

1237
00:43:15.524 --> 00:43:18.170
The idea that you don't have to compromise that, right?

1238
00:43:18.170 --> 00:43:19.003
Yeah, and I think

1239
00:43:19.003 --> 00:43:20.710
that's kind of what this book has shown

1240
00:43:20.710 --> 00:43:24.310
more than this is the trick to becoming a great athlete.

1241
00:43:24.310 --> 00:43:26.060
That's not really what this is about.

1242
00:43:26.060 --> 00:43:28.250
It turns out that it is that for the right person

1243
00:43:28.250 --> 00:43:30.510
and there are lots of people who, including all of us,

1244
00:43:30.510 --> 00:43:32.810
I think, who've kind of experienced

1245
00:43:32.810 --> 00:43:34.630
the most success we had athletically

1246
00:43:34.630 --> 00:43:35.923
once we went plant-based.

1247
00:43:37.010 --> 00:43:38.670
But for me, it's more that

1248
00:43:38.670 --> 00:43:41.290
you can do this and you can get all these great benefits

1249
00:43:41.290 --> 00:43:44.080
of the longevity, really, and health span.

1250
00:43:44.080 --> 00:43:46.857
To me, that's what it's all about.

1251
00:43:48.005 --> 00:43:50.270
You mentioned the omnivorous diet,

1252
00:43:50.270 --> 00:43:51.103
what's wrong with this.

1253
00:43:51.103 --> 00:43:52.040
This is natural,

1254
00:43:52.040 --> 00:43:54.540
but natural doesn't really affect,

1255
00:43:54.540 --> 00:43:55.820
it doesn't really get into health, right?

1256
00:43:55.820 --> 00:43:58.367
Nature selects for reaching reproductive age

1257
00:43:58.367 --> 00:44:00.380
and a few years past to raise your kids,

1258
00:44:00.380 --> 00:44:03.250
but it's not really about what gets you to 80, 90

1259
00:44:03.250 --> 00:44:04.660
and keep moving and being healthy

1260
00:44:04.660 --> 00:44:07.490
'cause that doesn't matter fr natural selection.

1261
00:44:07.490 --> 00:44:09.360
So, to me, that's where we should think

1262
00:44:09.360 --> 00:44:10.610
about not what is,

1263
00:44:10.610 --> 00:44:12.820
and I don't honestly know what is the most natural diet

1264
00:44:12.820 --> 00:44:14.223
or whatever that even means,

1265
00:44:15.720 --> 00:44:18.330
but which one is the data saying is keeping people,

1266
00:44:18.330 --> 00:44:19.870
giving them the longest health span,

1267
00:44:19.870 --> 00:44:22.247
keeping them mobile and happy and active

1268
00:44:22.247 --> 00:44:23.830
and healthy and alive?

1269
00:44:23.830 --> 00:44:25.150
And it looks a lot to me

1270
00:44:25.150 --> 00:44:26.530
like that's the plant-based diet

1271
00:44:26.530 --> 00:44:28.530
that seems to be where the science

1272
00:44:28.530 --> 00:44:29.730
is all pointing these days.

1273
00:44:29.730 --> 00:44:33.980
Right, you're on-ramp.

1274
00:44:33.980 --> 00:44:36.550
Robert was ethics.

1275
00:44:36.550 --> 00:44:38.440
Matt, yours was more health-related.

1276
00:44:38.440 --> 00:44:40.093
Mine was vanity.

1277
00:44:40.093 --> 00:44:40.926
(laughs)

1278
00:44:40.926 --> 00:44:43.840
Vanity and health and athletic performance ultimately,

1279
00:44:43.840 --> 00:44:45.660
but what's so amazing and beautiful

1280
00:44:45.660 --> 00:44:47.980
about how this movement has blossomed

1281
00:44:47.980 --> 00:44:50.160
is that now there are all these on-ramps

1282
00:44:50.160 --> 00:44:53.350
from the ethical considerations, of course,

1283
00:44:53.350 --> 00:44:56.550
to sustainability, to climate change concerns,

1284
00:44:56.550 --> 00:44:59.750
environmentally sensitive,

1285
00:44:59.750 --> 00:45:01.633
which we all should be, of course,

1286
00:45:02.730 --> 00:45:05.880
and the longevity health considerations

1287
00:45:05.880 --> 00:45:07.050
of the foods that we eat

1288
00:45:07.050 --> 00:45:11.900
and now with this book plant-based athletic performance

1289
00:45:11.900 --> 00:45:13.070
and I think it's so great

1290
00:45:13.070 --> 00:45:17.000
because just like all the athletes profiled in your book,

1291
00:45:17.000 --> 00:45:19.770
different people connect with and resonate

1292
00:45:19.770 --> 00:45:21.430
with different individuals, right?

1293
00:45:21.430 --> 00:45:23.940
So, not everybody is gonna cotton

1294
00:45:23.940 --> 00:45:25.450
onto the ethical argument,

1295
00:45:25.450 --> 00:45:27.770
but perhaps they're concerned about the environment

1296
00:45:27.770 --> 00:45:30.060
and the way that I look at it,

1297
00:45:30.060 --> 00:45:34.260
I look at it as this umbrella lifestyle

1298
00:45:34.260 --> 00:45:36.400
that checks every single box.

1299
00:45:36.400 --> 00:45:39.310
You can opt out of the chronic lifestyle illnesses

1300
00:45:39.310 --> 00:45:42.310
that are unnecessarily killing millions of people.

1301
00:45:42.310 --> 00:45:44.401
Obesity rates right now are through the roof.

1302
00:45:44.401 --> 00:45:48.130
Diabetes, it's predicted something like 50% of Americans

1303
00:45:48.130 --> 00:45:50.870
are gonna be diabetic by 2030.

1304
00:45:50.870 --> 00:45:54.320
All of these chronic illnesses are lifestyle illnesses

1305
00:45:54.320 --> 00:45:56.820
directly correlated to the foods that we're eating.

1306
00:45:56.820 --> 00:45:58.731
Meanwhile, we're decimating the planet

1307
00:45:58.731 --> 00:46:02.560
because animal agriculture just requires too many inputs,

1308
00:46:02.560 --> 00:46:04.860
too much land, too many resources

1309
00:46:04.860 --> 00:46:08.590
for us to sustainably produce enough animal products

1310
00:46:08.590 --> 00:46:09.900
for the planet to eat

1311
00:46:09.900 --> 00:46:14.530
as we careen down this path towards 10 billion people

1312
00:46:14.530 --> 00:46:15.803
living on this planet.

1313
00:46:17.058 --> 00:46:21.440
The truth is most people are walking around

1314
00:46:21.440 --> 00:46:22.770
thinking about themselves.

1315
00:46:22.770 --> 00:46:24.200
They're like, that's fine

1316
00:46:24.200 --> 00:46:25.900
but I just want to be buffed

1317
00:46:25.900 --> 00:46:27.910
and I wanna eat what I wanna eat

1318
00:46:27.910 --> 00:46:29.790
and I wanna be able to kill it in the gym

1319
00:46:29.790 --> 00:46:33.380
or qualify for Boston or whatever it is.

1320
00:46:33.380 --> 00:46:36.150
And the truth is that all of those goals

1321
00:46:36.150 --> 00:46:39.400
are not just possible, but more possible

1322
00:46:39.400 --> 00:46:41.360
by dent of learning

1323
00:46:41.360 --> 00:46:44.100
what you guys have laid out in this book.

1324
00:46:44.100 --> 00:46:45.770
When you read the stories,

