Matt and I went to a soccer game.

2367
01:23:26.190 --> 01:23:28.810
We met up in person to work on some of the book aspects

2368
01:23:28.810 --> 01:23:30.530
and Holden then was a schooling,

2369
01:23:30.530 --> 01:23:33.420
everybody on the field during halftime with this like

2370
01:23:33.420 --> 01:23:34.700
semi-pro game or something.

2371
01:23:34.700 --> 01:23:37.720
And I've known Holden since he was born.

2372
01:23:37.720 --> 01:23:38.800
Yeah, that's right.

2373
01:23:38.800 --> 01:23:40.540
So, we go back a long way.

2374
01:23:40.540 --> 01:23:42.287
But anyway, someone saw his Instagram

2375
01:23:42.287 --> 01:23:44.300
and they were making fun of him or something

2376
01:23:44.300 --> 01:23:45.133
during a practice.

2377
01:23:45.133 --> 01:23:46.530
And it was the only time I've really ever

2378
01:23:46.530 --> 01:23:47.720
dealt with anything like that,

2379
01:23:47.720 --> 01:23:49.910
where he told me in the car and he was sort of embarrassed

2380
01:23:49.910 --> 01:23:51.180
that it had happened.

2381
01:23:51.180 --> 01:23:52.542
And I was like, oh, I mean, whatever.

2382
01:23:52.542 --> 01:23:55.310
And we just talked about it and it lasted about 10 minutes.

2383
01:23:55.310 --> 01:23:56.860
And then the next time he didn't care.

2384
01:23:56.860 --> 01:23:58.020
They're so comfortable with it

2385
01:23:58.020 --> 01:24:00.640
because they know that's what I do.

2386
01:24:00.640 --> 01:24:03.990
It's a very much part of their being.

2387
01:24:03.990 --> 01:24:05.980
It's not like just the thing we're trying that's weird

2388
01:24:05.980 --> 01:24:07.728
and they're ready to ditch it whenever.

2389
01:24:07.728 --> 01:24:09.186
They know it's--

2390
01:24:09.186 --> 01:24:10.100
They're into it.

2391
01:24:10.100 --> 01:24:12.570
Yeah, so to be made fun of for 10 minutes

2392
01:24:12.570 --> 01:24:13.403
doesn't really matter.

2393
01:24:13.403 --> 01:24:14.236
That's cool.

2394
01:24:14.236 --> 01:24:15.900
That's no small feat.

2395
01:24:15.900 --> 01:24:20.900
I feel like kids either define themselves

2396
01:24:20.960 --> 01:24:24.030
in terms of trying to like live up to the example

2397
01:24:24.030 --> 01:24:24.930
their parents set,

2398
01:24:24.930 --> 01:24:29.630
or they sort of push the boundaries and try to figure out

2399
01:24:29.630 --> 01:24:33.240
who they are by defining themselves

2400
01:24:33.240 --> 01:24:34.810
in opposition to their parents.

2401
01:24:34.810 --> 01:24:37.367
We're dealing with a little of that right now.

2402
01:24:37.367 --> 01:24:40.300
So, maybe that's coming, but from the beginning,

2403
01:24:40.300 --> 01:24:41.430
I've said to them,

2404
01:24:41.430 --> 01:24:43.500
we're not gonna cook it in the house,

2405
01:24:43.500 --> 01:24:46.040
but if you guys want to have a hamburger one day, tell me.

2406
01:24:46.040 --> 01:24:48.720
I'm not here to limit your joy.

2407
01:24:48.720 --> 01:24:51.070
I know in some capacity I am,

2408
01:24:51.070 --> 01:24:52.917
if they started eating that stuff routinely, I would say,

2409
01:24:52.917 --> 01:24:55.310
"I don't think this is the healthiest thing you could do,"

2410
01:24:55.310 --> 01:24:57.870
but I don't want to dictate their ethics and say,

2411
01:24:57.870 --> 01:24:59.370
you're not allowed to do this.

2412
01:24:59.370 --> 01:25:00.600
So I said, if you ever want that,

2413
01:25:00.600 --> 01:25:02.380
you tell me and we'll work that out.

2414
01:25:02.380 --> 01:25:03.713
I don't know how, but we'll do that.

2415
01:25:03.713 --> 01:25:06.540
I think that's a really important point.

2416
01:25:06.540 --> 01:25:08.440
That deserves a little bit of attention,

2417
01:25:08.440 --> 01:25:12.860
because I think by doing that you're basically accomplishing

2418
01:25:12.860 --> 01:25:13.693
a couple of things.

2419
01:25:13.693 --> 01:25:14.526
First of all,

2420
01:25:14.526 --> 01:25:19.420
you're removing all of the kind of tension around that idea,

2421
01:25:20.580 --> 01:25:22.460
because there's nothing to rebel against.

2422
01:25:22.460 --> 01:25:23.510
Right, you're like, one hamburger?

2423
01:25:23.510 --> 01:25:24.600
Here, I'll give you a hamburger, right?

2424
01:25:24.600 --> 01:25:27.850
So, they're not gonna get any rush out of being like,

2425
01:25:29.710 --> 01:25:31.486
I'm doing something wrong, right?

2426
01:25:31.486 --> 01:25:32.620
You're like, it's cool.

2427
01:25:32.620 --> 01:25:37.620
And secondarily, you're saying I'm not gonna get caught up

2428
01:25:37.740 --> 01:25:41.510
in the minutia of your daily choices.

2429
01:25:41.510 --> 01:25:45.440
What I'm interested in is creating a foundation of education

2430
01:25:45.440 --> 01:25:47.430
and healthy habits that will serve you

2431
01:25:47.430 --> 01:25:48.640
throughout the rest of your life.

2432
01:25:48.640 --> 01:25:49.940
It's not about that hamburger.

2433
01:25:49.940 --> 01:25:51.890
It's about how are you gonna be eating in five years,

2434
01:25:51.890 --> 01:25:53.870
10 years, 15 years from now.

2435
01:25:53.870 --> 01:25:54.950
Yap, exactly.

2436
01:25:54.950 --> 01:25:59.950
Yeah, back to a little bit of myth-busting

2437
01:26:00.550 --> 01:26:03.070
or just kind of top level subjects.

2438
01:26:03.070 --> 01:26:04.758
Another thing that comes up a lot,

2439
01:26:04.758 --> 01:26:08.500
I'm sure you fielded this inquiry frequently,

2440
01:26:08.500 --> 01:26:12.960
is, okay, maybe I could be interested in this,

2441
01:26:12.960 --> 01:26:14.940
but this sounds like a lot of work.

2442
01:26:14.940 --> 01:26:15.773
What am I gonna be?

2443
01:26:15.773 --> 01:26:18.520
In that kitchen all day long doing meal prep

2444
01:26:18.520 --> 01:26:20.470
and I'm gonna have to buy all these exotic foods

2445
01:26:20.470 --> 01:26:22.610
and I'm gonna have to be thinking about what I'm eating

2446
01:26:22.610 --> 01:26:24.110
all the time.

2447
01:26:24.110 --> 01:26:26.789
It's just I'm busy.

2448
01:26:26.789 --> 01:26:27.750
(chuckles)

2449
01:26:27.750 --> 01:26:31.520
Yeah, well, maybe I'm a good person to answer this because

2450
01:26:31.520 --> 01:26:32.980
I don't know how to cook anything

2451
01:26:32.980 --> 01:26:34.970
unlike you guys who have cookbooks.

2452
01:26:34.970 --> 01:26:36.200
I can't make anything,

2453
01:26:36.200 --> 01:26:38.232
and I've been doing this for 25 years.

2454
01:26:38.232 --> 01:26:40.760
So, it's totally easy for me.

2455
01:26:40.760 --> 01:26:42.180
Largely, I eat a lot of simple foods.

2456
01:26:42.180 --> 01:26:43.330
I eat a lot of produce.

2457
01:26:43.330 --> 01:26:46.370
I eat foods that I really enjoy, lots of different fruits

2458
01:26:46.370 --> 01:26:50.480
and foods that are already prepared.

2459
01:26:50.480 --> 01:26:53.910
I rolled into town and picked up some plant-based sushi,

2460
01:26:53.910 --> 01:26:55.570
whole foods market or I can get it anywhere.

2461
01:26:55.570 --> 01:26:58.160
It doesn't have to be in an elitist kind of store,

2462
01:26:58.160 --> 01:26:58.993
like whole foods.

2463
01:26:58.993 --> 01:27:00.020
It can be anywhere.

2464
01:27:00.020 --> 01:27:02.720
And just the accessibility

2465
01:27:02.720 --> 01:27:04.470
of anything that you already enjoy,

2466
01:27:04.470 --> 01:27:08.360
burritos, tacos, pizza, sandwiches,

2467
01:27:08.360 --> 01:27:13.100
wraps, salads, sushi, fur, whatever it is.

2468
01:27:13.100 --> 01:27:15.330
It's there, it's available.

2469
01:27:15.330 --> 01:27:19.610
And I'm someone who is a recovering workaholic.

2470
01:27:19.610 --> 01:27:22.020
I used to have to maximize every one

2471
01:27:22.020 --> 01:27:24.800
of the 1,440 minutes We have each day.

2472
01:27:24.800 --> 01:27:27.300
And that goes back to my early days of

2473
01:27:27.300 --> 01:27:28.620
hustle, hustle and grind.

2474
01:27:28.620 --> 01:27:31.370
Gary Vaynerchuk inspired in 2009 when I met him

2475
01:27:31.370 --> 01:27:34.120
and then used to kind of follow that crush at approach.

2476
01:27:34.961 --> 01:27:37.770
And even as someone who is obsessively busy,

2477
01:27:37.770 --> 01:27:40.140
it worked for me because I could just go down the street

2478
01:27:40.140 --> 01:27:41.690
to someplace and get a burrito,

2479
01:27:42.918 --> 01:27:44.040
or I'd have a bunch of fruit at home

2480
01:27:44.040 --> 01:27:45.600
and not just boring fruit.

2481
01:27:45.600 --> 01:27:46.450
At one time I counted,

2482
01:27:46.450 --> 01:27:49.530
I had 19 different types of fruit at home at one time.

2483
01:27:49.530 --> 01:27:52.880
And that can be berries and melons and citrus

2484
01:27:52.880 --> 01:27:54.680
and lots of different things, avocado.

2485
01:27:54.680 --> 01:27:55.737
And so, there's a variety of there.

2486
01:27:55.737 --> 01:27:57.136
You just grab them.

2487
01:27:57.136 --> 01:27:57.969
You grab some blueberries,

2488
01:27:57.969 --> 01:27:59.540
grab some raspberries, strawberries,

2489
01:27:59.540 --> 01:28:01.330
watermelon, pineapple, whatever

2490
01:28:01.330 --> 01:28:03.430
and then the heavier stuff.

2491
01:28:03.430 --> 01:28:05.340
It doesn't really take much work.

2492
01:28:05.340 --> 01:28:06.173
I say I can't cook,

2493
01:28:06.173 --> 01:28:08.590
but I obviously know how to make rice or pasta

2494
01:28:08.590 --> 01:28:09.423
and those kinda things.

2495
01:28:09.423 --> 01:28:10.256
So, it can be staples.

2496
01:28:10.256 --> 01:28:11.089
They're heavier,

2497
01:28:11.089 --> 01:28:11.922
more calorie dense,

2498
01:28:11.922 --> 01:28:12.930
you add other things to them.

2499
01:28:12.930 --> 01:28:15.460
Some olives, some sauce, whatever.

2500
01:28:15.460 --> 01:28:16.673
The point is,

2501
01:28:17.660 --> 01:28:20.143
it's more accessible now than ever before.

2502
01:28:21.130 --> 01:28:24.780
I'm sure that's just on repeat now.

2503
01:28:24.780 --> 01:28:25.720
Everyone's repeating that.

2504
01:28:25.720 --> 01:28:27.820
You can just get fast food places.

2505
01:28:27.820 --> 01:28:29.580
Not that we're encouraging people to eat fast food,

2506
01:28:29.580 --> 01:28:31.534
but the accessibility of a plant-based diet

2507
01:28:31.534 --> 01:28:34.320
has never been greater than it is today.

2508
01:28:34.320 --> 01:28:36.000
And it doesn't have to be exotic.

2509
01:28:36.000 --> 01:28:37.630
Doesn't have to be expensive.

2510
01:28:37.630 --> 01:28:39.840
And you just go down the street

2511
01:28:39.840 --> 01:28:41.690
and find some great vegan foods.

2512
01:28:41.690 --> 01:28:44.280
Yeah, the floor for me is always,

2513
01:28:44.280 --> 01:28:46.350
at least within United States.

2514
01:28:46.350 --> 01:28:48.930
I know that pretty much every city I go to,

2515
01:28:48.930 --> 01:28:51.630
there's gonna be a Chipotle and I can get a burrito bowl

2516
01:28:51.630 --> 01:28:54.600
or vegan burrito bowl, vegan burrito.

2517
01:28:54.600 --> 01:28:56.900
So, it doesn't matter where I'm headed.

2518
01:28:56.900 --> 01:28:58.233
If I'm headed to a city,

2519
01:28:58.233 --> 01:28:59.870
I don't have to think about it.

2520
01:28:59.870 --> 01:29:01.140
There's always that.

2521
01:29:01.140 --> 01:29:03.130
If I can't find something else,

2522
01:29:03.130 --> 01:29:05.734
I'll always be able to feed myself there.

2523
01:29:05.734 --> 01:29:06.590
(laughs)

2524
01:29:06.590 --> 01:29:08.610
Yeah, and now with Taco Bell,

2525
01:29:08.610 --> 01:29:09.443
it's not the healthiest,

2526
01:29:09.443 --> 01:29:11.009
but there are a lot of good vegan options there.

2527
01:29:11.009 --> 01:29:11.842
If you want something different--

2528
01:29:11.842 --> 01:29:12.675
Are there?

2529
01:29:12.675 --> 01:29:13.508
Oh, tons.

2530
01:29:13.508 --> 01:29:14.570
Yeah, like black bean, anything now.

2531
01:29:14.570 --> 01:29:15.403
In Taco Bell..

2532
01:29:15.403 --> 01:29:16.546
That's what I was gonna say.

2533
01:29:16.546 --> 01:29:17.379
That was the staple in the '90s

2534
01:29:17.379 --> 01:29:18.650
was Taco Bell before Chipotle.

2535
01:29:18.650 --> 01:29:20.121
That's where the vegans met.

2536
01:29:20.121 --> 01:29:21.250
Well, here's the danger, though,

2537
01:29:21.250 --> 01:29:22.880
and maybe we could talk about this for a couple of minutes,

2538
01:29:22.880 --> 01:29:24.750
which is, and you alluded to this

2539
01:29:24.750 --> 01:29:26.620
at the beginning of the conversation

2540
01:29:26.620 --> 01:29:30.740
because plant-based vegan eating has become so popular

2541
01:29:30.740 --> 01:29:33.120
and we have food scientists

2542
01:29:33.120 --> 01:29:36.740
who figured out how to make plant based analogs

2543
01:29:36.740 --> 01:29:39.360
to all our favorite animal product foods.

2544
01:29:39.360 --> 01:29:41.230
There is just a proliferation

2545
01:29:41.230 --> 01:29:43.960
of vegan junk food everywhere you look

2546
01:29:43.960 --> 01:29:46.910
to the point where almost every single fast food restaurant

2547
01:29:46.910 --> 01:29:49.930
has a Beyond Meat or an Impossible Burger.

2548
01:29:49.930 --> 01:29:51.830
So, you could literally just go back

2549
01:29:51.830 --> 01:29:55.207
to being that drive-thru guy and say,

2550
01:29:55.207 --> 01:29:56.650
"I'm vegan and I'm healthy,"

2551
01:29:56.650 --> 01:30:00.210
when you're truly, really, if we're being honest,

2552
01:30:00.210 --> 01:30:01.600
not eating any better than you were

2553
01:30:01.600 --> 01:30:03.600
when you were on the junk food diet.

2554
01:30:03.600 --> 01:30:06.610
Which I think that's a very real concern.

2555
01:30:06.610 --> 01:30:08.530
It's cool that so much of the population

2556
01:30:08.530 --> 01:30:10.637
is now able to incorporate more plant-based foods.

2557
01:30:10.637 --> 01:30:13.300
And I think something like 60 or 70% of people

2558
01:30:13.300 --> 01:30:14.780
in surveys say they are incorporating

2559
01:30:14.780 --> 01:30:16.410
more plant-based foods now.

2560
01:30:16.410 --> 01:30:17.243
That's awesome.

2561
01:30:17.243 --> 01:30:18.480
It's great for animals.

2562
01:30:18.480 --> 01:30:19.780
Yeah, from an ethical

2563
01:30:19.780 --> 01:30:22.210
and environmental perspective, fantastic.

2564
01:30:22.210 --> 01:30:25.350
Right, and for the time being, that's a good thing.

2565
01:30:25.350 --> 01:30:26.730
What I wonder about,

2566
01:30:26.730 --> 01:30:27.750
and my friend Ray Kornheiser

2567
01:30:27.750 --> 01:30:29.540
has suggested this to me a long time ago

2568
01:30:29.540 --> 01:30:31.960
is what happens when they start studying people

2569
01:30:31.960 --> 01:30:35.820
who eat "plant-based diets" 10, 15 years from now,

2570
01:30:35.820 --> 01:30:37.720
when people are doing what you just described.

2571
01:30:37.720 --> 01:30:39.337
They're eating the junk food standard American diet,

2572
01:30:39.337 --> 01:30:41.190
just a vegan version of it.

2573
01:30:41.190 --> 01:30:42.663
And then the headlines are

2574
01:30:42.663 --> 01:30:43.620
plant-based diet

2575
01:30:43.620 --> 01:30:44.598
doesn't, actually, work.
Plant-based diet

2576
01:30:44.598 --> 01:30:45.431
doesn't work.

2577
01:30:45.431 --> 01:30:46.264
Yeah, (chuckles) exactly.

2578
01:30:46.264 --> 01:30:49.180
So, I think that's a real danger as great as it all is

2579
01:30:49.180 --> 01:30:50.510
as much as these conveniences are nice

2580
01:30:50.510 --> 01:30:52.180
for people who are kind of already in

2581
01:30:52.180 --> 01:30:54.900
and I think certainly it's gonna create a bunch of vegans

2582
01:30:54.900 --> 01:30:56.550
who, or I shouldn't say vegans,

2583
01:30:56.550 --> 01:30:57.500
plant-based eaters,

2584
01:30:57.500 --> 01:30:59.000
who are part-time plant-based eaters,

2585
01:30:59.000 --> 01:31:00.770
who get into it and then they realize

2586
01:31:00.770 --> 01:31:02.840
via the Impossible Whopper or whatever

2587
01:31:02.840 --> 01:31:06.320
that they actually really like thinking about their food

2588
01:31:06.320 --> 01:31:08.870
and that's just their very, very first step

2589
01:31:08.870 --> 01:31:10.240
when they might not have imagined

2590
01:31:10.240 --> 01:31:11.630
being able to do this before,

2591
01:31:11.630 --> 01:31:13.931
but then two or three years from now,

2592
01:31:13.931 --> 01:31:16.590
they are doing all the work you just described.

2593
01:31:16.590 --> 01:31:18.910
Yes, it is a lot of work to really eat healthily

2594
01:31:18.910 --> 01:31:21.230
and to make food, I don't wanna say your hobby,

2595
01:31:21.230 --> 01:31:23.510
but one of the important pillars of your life

2596
01:31:23.510 --> 01:31:25.240
is putting good food on the table

2597
01:31:25.240 --> 01:31:27.210
or getting it in the car for a soccer trip

2598
01:31:27.210 --> 01:31:29.492
or getting it in your kids or whatever.

2599
01:31:29.492 --> 01:31:30.800
That's real work

2600
01:31:30.800 --> 01:31:33.258
and I think the way to get to that

2601
01:31:33.258 --> 01:31:34.840
really is like any other.

2602
01:31:34.840 --> 01:31:37.530
I'd be like, if you are super into gonna the gym

2603
01:31:37.530 --> 01:31:38.640
and you know all these different lifts

2604
01:31:38.640 --> 01:31:41.230
and you know where you stand with each of those lifts

2605
01:31:41.230 --> 01:31:43.080
and you know your personal best,

2606
01:31:43.080 --> 01:31:44.210
that also took a lot of work

2607
01:31:44.210 --> 01:31:46.533
to get that level of development.

2608
01:31:47.370 --> 01:31:48.210
It's the same way with food,

2609
01:31:48.210 --> 01:31:50.210
but you kinda start right where you are.

2610
01:31:51.300 --> 01:31:52.480
If you're inspired, then sure,

2611
01:31:52.480 --> 01:31:53.380
go plant-based overnight,

2612
01:31:53.380 --> 01:31:54.350
just see what happens,

2613
01:31:54.350 --> 01:31:55.183
but if it doesn't work,

2614
01:31:55.183 --> 01:31:56.650
which in many, many cases, it won't

2615
01:31:56.650 --> 01:31:58.634
because it's such a drastic shift,

2616
01:31:58.634 --> 01:32:00.970
then do the small steps approach.

2617
01:32:00.970 --> 01:32:02.520
Start with just breakfast,

2618
01:32:02.520 --> 01:32:04.550
do that for two weeks, if you want,

2619
01:32:04.550 --> 01:32:07.690
and then maybe start pushing the line

2620
01:32:07.690 --> 01:32:09.190
to later and later in the day.

2621
01:32:10.040 --> 01:32:11.150
But I just think starting where you are

2622
01:32:11.150 --> 01:32:14.600
and kinda letting it become almost like a hobby for you,

2623
01:32:14.600 --> 01:32:15.433
