01:48:58.384 --> 01:48:59.520
and I was using the StairMaster

3145
01:48:59.520 --> 01:49:00.650
and I was doing fasted, cardio,

3146
01:49:00.650 --> 01:49:03.040
all the stuff I used to do in my 20's and 30's,

3147
01:49:03.040 --> 01:49:05.763
and I wasn't seeing the results quite as fast.

3148
01:49:06.730 --> 01:49:09.320
And I feel like there's a couple of factors at play.

3149
01:49:09.320 --> 01:49:13.480
One, stress and anxiety, which I suffer a lot from,

3150
01:49:13.480 --> 01:49:14.980
including coming on the show.

3151
01:49:14.980 --> 01:49:16.777
It was weeks of worry.

3152
01:49:16.777 --> 01:49:17.900
(chuckles)

3153
01:49:17.900 --> 01:49:18.733
Oh, come on.

3154
01:49:18.733 --> 01:49:19.566
And that, man, is the truth.

3155
01:49:19.566 --> 01:49:20.399
That's just the truth.

3156
01:49:20.399 --> 01:49:23.386
And so, that impacts me a little bit.

3157
01:49:23.386 --> 01:49:26.500
And then working with Vegan Strong,

3158
01:49:26.500 --> 01:49:27.886
is a nonprofit that I'm part of

3159
01:49:27.886 --> 01:49:30.913
and launching a book that we hope becomes the best seller,

3160
01:49:31.750 --> 01:49:33.190
it's time consuming

3161
01:49:33.190 --> 01:49:36.440
and then taking care of two dogs

3162
01:49:36.440 --> 01:49:38.950
and making sure I hang out with my wife

3163
01:49:38.950 --> 01:49:41.843
and make sure I'm social in some capacity,

3164
01:49:42.980 --> 01:49:45.410
the discipline has been there.

3165
01:49:45.410 --> 01:49:46.930
I'm still getting a lot of good exercise in,

3166
01:49:46.930 --> 01:49:48.090
but sometimes the results

3167
01:49:48.090 --> 01:49:50.880
have been a little bit slower recently, it feels like,

3168
01:49:50.880 --> 01:49:51.713
but at the same time,

3169
01:49:51.713 --> 01:49:53.090
if I get in the right lighting,

3170
01:49:53.090 --> 01:49:56.070
I take my little photos you see on Instagram

3171
01:49:56.070 --> 01:49:57.120
with me in the mirror

3172
01:49:57.970 --> 01:49:59.531
and I'm the biggest.
I've seen them.

3173
01:49:59.531 --> 01:50:00.792
Yeah, there's some of the best shape I've ever been in.

3174
01:50:00.792 --> 01:50:01.813
Everybody's has seen them.

3175
01:50:01.813 --> 01:50:02.727
What's that?

3176
01:50:02.727 --> 01:50:03.560
Everybody's seen them.

3177
01:50:03.560 --> 01:50:04.393
Yeah.

3178
01:50:04.393 --> 01:50:05.226
That's Robert Cheeke.

3179
01:50:05.226 --> 01:50:06.059
That's your thing, dude.

3180
01:50:06.059 --> 01:50:06.892
And I'm surprise you even wear a tank top.

3181
01:50:06.892 --> 01:50:08.877
Yeah, that's me and my smiling thumbs up

3182
01:50:08.877 --> 01:50:10.660
and the side pose,

3183
01:50:10.660 --> 01:50:12.673
but obviously I'm playing to my strengths.

3184
01:50:13.530 --> 01:50:15.743
I've focused on the muscle groups that look the best.

3185
01:50:15.743 --> 01:50:18.070
It's all part of this ego thing

3186
01:50:18.070 --> 01:50:19.750
that Matt and I talked about for an hour and a half

3187
01:50:19.750 --> 01:50:20.583
at dinner last night

3188
01:50:20.583 --> 01:50:23.180
is trying to overcome and let go of some of those things

3189
01:50:23.180 --> 01:50:26.810
of who we were a decade ago versus who we are now

3190
01:50:26.810 --> 01:50:30.150
and where we are within the movement 10 years ago,

3191
01:50:30.150 --> 01:50:31.370
compared to where we are now

3192
01:50:31.370 --> 01:50:33.950
and that wrestling match.

3193
01:50:33.950 --> 01:50:37.293
Yeah, no, I relate to that a lot.

3194
01:50:38.680 --> 01:50:41.190
Coming up on 55 pretty quick here

3195
01:50:41.190 --> 01:50:43.270
and one of the things that I've done during quarantine

3196
01:50:43.270 --> 01:50:45.010
is something that I haven't done in a very long time,

3197
01:50:45.010 --> 01:50:47.330
which is to focus on strength.

3198
01:50:47.330 --> 01:50:49.869
And I got back into the gym

3199
01:50:49.869 --> 01:50:52.710
and I have no problem putting on mass.

3200
01:50:52.710 --> 01:50:54.520
It happens (snaps) like that for me,

3201
01:50:54.520 --> 01:50:57.000
like almost too quickly,

3202
01:50:57.000 --> 01:50:58.490
but I was bulking up

3203
01:50:58.490 --> 01:50:59.620
and then I just didn't like how...

3204
01:50:59.620 --> 01:51:00.710
I felt good.

3205
01:51:00.710 --> 01:51:01.673
I felt strong,

3206
01:51:02.951 --> 01:51:04.490
but I just felt bulky

3207
01:51:04.490 --> 01:51:07.023
and I've kind of backed off a little bit.

3208
01:51:09.410 --> 01:51:13.780
It's fine if I pair that with some pretty decent volume

3209
01:51:13.780 --> 01:51:15.630
in terms of my endurance training

3210
01:51:15.630 --> 01:51:18.003
'cause I can maintain being lean,

3211
01:51:19.200 --> 01:51:21.990
but I'm not able to train that much right now

3212
01:51:21.990 --> 01:51:24.760
because of all the things that I have going on right now.

3213
01:51:24.760 --> 01:51:26.140
And so, I've kind of pivoted back

3214
01:51:26.140 --> 01:51:29.300
towards the running and the cycling and things like that

3215
01:51:29.300 --> 01:51:31.700
'cause I just felt like I was starting to feel

3216
01:51:31.700 --> 01:51:33.210
like the Michelin man a little bit.

3217
01:51:33.210 --> 01:51:35.350
So, I guess what I'm saying is that

3218
01:51:35.350 --> 01:51:40.300
I noticed that I can't shift gears in the way that I could

3219
01:51:40.300 --> 01:51:41.270
maybe 10 years ago

3220
01:51:41.270 --> 01:51:44.590
in terms of oh, I wanna put bulk on

3221
01:51:44.590 --> 01:51:46.300
and then I wanna lean out.

3222
01:51:46.300 --> 01:51:47.680
I can still do all those things,

3223
01:51:47.680 --> 01:51:52.240
but I need to bank more time in order to achieve those goals

3224
01:51:52.240 --> 01:51:56.283
versus the way that it was maybe a decade ago.

3225
01:51:57.140 --> 01:51:57.973
I've noticed exactly,

3226
01:51:57.973 --> 01:51:59.190
with the quarantine period,

3227
01:51:59.190 --> 01:52:02.460
like a lot of people, I did all kinds of cooking.

3228
01:52:02.460 --> 01:52:03.400
It was crazy.

3229
01:52:03.400 --> 01:52:06.103
I had so much fun with all that extra family time,

3230
01:52:07.110 --> 01:52:09.540
but just started eating junk food

3231
01:52:09.540 --> 01:52:10.580
and I kept telling myself,

3232
01:52:10.580 --> 01:52:11.987
well, I eat a vegan diet.

3233
01:52:11.987 --> 01:52:13.950
So, it's not really a problem.

3234
01:52:13.950 --> 01:52:14.783
I can't gain weight

3235
01:52:14.783 --> 01:52:15.704
and I'm always said

3236
01:52:15.704 --> 01:52:18.240
I don't really put on mass or get fat or anything,

3237
01:52:18.240 --> 01:52:21.430
but I had turned 40 a couple months ago

3238
01:52:21.430 --> 01:52:23.650
and it's just a little bit different now

3239
01:52:23.650 --> 01:52:24.980
and a lot of things are different.

3240
01:52:24.980 --> 01:52:26.737
I don't sleep like I used to.

3241
01:52:26.737 --> 01:52:30.370
I've had to get the blackout curtains

3242
01:52:30.370 --> 01:52:32.630
and get the little thing

3243
01:52:32.630 --> 01:52:34.210
where it cools your mattress at night

3244
01:52:34.210 --> 01:52:35.460
so that you don't wake up.

3245
01:52:35.460 --> 01:52:37.410
I'm sorry to do like wacky sleep.

3246
01:52:37.410 --> 01:52:38.700
Yeah, me too.

3247
01:52:38.700 --> 01:52:40.320
All the things that just came easy naturally

3248
01:52:40.320 --> 01:52:42.090
now you gotta work for them.

3249
01:52:42.090 --> 01:52:43.359
Exactly, so now I'm like,

3250
01:52:43.359 --> 01:52:44.430
well, I don't wanna eat a meal too close to bedtime

3251
01:52:44.430 --> 01:52:45.600
'cause that'll mess up my sleep

3252
01:52:45.600 --> 01:52:47.490
and partly because now I'm paying attention to the data,

3253
01:52:47.490 --> 01:52:48.773
which drives me nuts.

3254
01:52:49.800 --> 01:52:50.850
You got the Oura ring on you?

3255
01:52:50.850 --> 01:52:51.727
Yeah, I got it.

3256
01:52:51.727 --> 01:52:52.560
I need this data.

3257
01:52:52.560 --> 01:52:53.590
I can't lose this hour.

3258
01:52:53.590 --> 01:52:55.300
But then the data can with your head.

3259
01:52:55.300 --> 01:52:56.430
Oh, my gosh.

3260
01:52:56.430 --> 01:52:57.440
It really can.

3261
01:52:57.440 --> 01:52:58.650
I think it's a good thing,

3262
01:52:58.650 --> 01:53:00.610
but I think we haven't quite figured out

3263
01:53:00.610 --> 01:53:02.940
how to best live with it yet.

3264
01:53:02.940 --> 01:53:04.000
Anyway, I just think, yeah,

3265
01:53:04.000 --> 01:53:07.510
the changes are a little bit slower to happen.

3266
01:53:07.510 --> 01:53:11.460
But for me it's kind of a reason to get back into it

3267
01:53:11.460 --> 01:53:13.780
'cause it's like suddenly I can't just go on autopilot

3268
01:53:13.780 --> 01:53:15.080
and say, well I eat vegan.

3269
01:53:15.080 --> 01:53:16.120
So, I don't need to think about it.

3270
01:53:16.120 --> 01:53:17.960
And I was falling into that for awhile.

3271
01:53:17.960 --> 01:53:20.770
And then I actually did some heart health numbers

3272
01:53:20.770 --> 01:53:22.010
and they weren't all that good

3273
01:53:22.010 --> 01:53:23.330
'cause I've been in the Impossible Burgers

3274
01:53:23.330 --> 01:53:24.900
with all the soccer driving

3275
01:53:24.900 --> 01:53:27.567
and whatever else, just potato chips and just things

3276
01:53:27.567 --> 01:53:29.750
and I just kept telling myself, well, it's vegan.

3277
01:53:29.750 --> 01:53:31.230
So, I'll be fine

3278
01:53:31.230 --> 01:53:33.083
'cause I'm the vegan, healthy guy.

3279
01:53:34.430 --> 01:53:37.403
But seeing that, and it's not like they were scary numbers,

3280
01:53:37.403 --> 01:53:38.236
but it was like,

3281
01:53:38.236 --> 01:53:40.970
wow, this is not a trajectory I wanna keep going down.

3282
01:53:40.970 --> 01:53:44.323
So, it's been a really big boost for me

3283
01:53:44.323 --> 01:53:46.310
to say, wow, I'm 40 now.

3284
01:53:46.310 --> 01:53:48.520
It's a little bit different era for me.

3285
01:53:48.520 --> 01:53:50.714
And when I hit 50,

3286
01:53:50.714 --> 01:53:51.820
it'd be really cool

3287
01:53:51.820 --> 01:53:54.010
if I was in totally great control of this stuff.

3288
01:53:54.010 --> 01:53:57.280
So, I really got reinvigorated in the past few months

3289
01:53:57.280 --> 01:53:58.540
before all this stuff.

3290
01:53:58.540 --> 01:54:02.412
Let's talk a little bit about advocacy.

3291
01:54:02.412 --> 01:54:03.245
(sighs)

3292
01:54:03.245 --> 01:54:04.440
We alluded earlier

3293
01:54:04.440 --> 01:54:08.200
to sort of some infighting and the vegan movement.

3294
01:54:08.200 --> 01:54:10.410
There's a lot of sniping going on

3295
01:54:10.410 --> 01:54:12.510
and I spent a lot of time thinking about

3296
01:54:12.510 --> 01:54:16.647
how to be an advocate for the things that I believe in

3297
01:54:16.647 --> 01:54:18.470
and things that I care about.

3298
01:54:18.470 --> 01:54:19.867
And if you take

3299
01:54:19.867 --> 01:54:23.020
the Plant-based Athlete Movement as an example,

3300
01:54:23.020 --> 01:54:25.740
you'll see a spectrum of different strategies

3301
01:54:25.740 --> 01:54:29.140
from the super hardcore animal rights advocate

3302
01:54:29.140 --> 01:54:31.490
who is taking new prisoners

3303
01:54:31.490 --> 01:54:33.570
to the very gentle approach, Matt,

3304
01:54:33.570 --> 01:54:35.160
that I think you've adopted

3305
01:54:35.160 --> 01:54:38.290
and that is kind of in tune with your constitution.

3306
01:54:38.290 --> 01:54:39.780
It just feels very authentic to you.

3307
01:54:39.780 --> 01:54:40.830
If I had to say,

3308
01:54:40.830 --> 01:54:45.490
I'm more in your kind of side of that spectrum.

3309
01:54:45.490 --> 01:54:47.170
And I tend to think of it

3310
01:54:47.170 --> 01:54:51.610
as just trying to be an optimal living example

3311
01:54:51.610 --> 01:54:53.590
of the values and the ideals

3312
01:54:53.590 --> 01:54:54.890
that I care about

3313
01:54:54.890 --> 01:54:56.300
but I think it is really important

3314
01:54:56.300 --> 01:55:00.780
to be mindful about how we communicate these values.

3315
01:55:00.780 --> 01:55:03.650
To do it in a way that it connects and resonates

3316
01:55:03.650 --> 01:55:06.600
with as many people as possible.

3317
01:55:06.600 --> 01:55:09.720
So, Robert, how do you think about that?

3318
01:55:09.720 --> 01:55:11.930
It almost sounds cliche,

3319
01:55:11.930 --> 01:55:13.330
but I like the expression

3320
01:55:13.330 --> 01:55:17.550
that I'm in constant pursuit of the best version of myself,

3321
01:55:17.550 --> 01:55:18.559
but that's true.

3322
01:55:18.559 --> 01:55:21.010
That really is true

3323
01:55:21.010 --> 01:55:22.570
because I got into this

3324
01:55:22.570 --> 01:55:23.810
because I wanted to make a difference

3325
01:55:23.810 --> 01:55:24.650
in the world around me.

3326
01:55:24.650 --> 01:55:26.677
I wanted to make a difference to the farm animals

3327
01:55:26.677 --> 01:55:28.081
that I was around

3328
01:55:28.081 --> 01:55:31.380
and later I wanted to inspire people.

3329
01:55:31.380 --> 01:55:35.100
I really truly wanted and want to make a difference.

3330
01:55:35.100 --> 01:55:37.330
And whether that's because it makes me feel significant

3331
01:55:37.330 --> 01:55:38.650
or it makes me feel fulfilled

3332
01:55:38.650 --> 01:55:40.780
or that my life has purpose

3333
01:55:40.780 --> 01:55:43.220
because I'm significant in the life of somebody else,

3334
01:55:43.220 --> 01:55:44.527
even someone who just read a book and said,

3335
01:55:44.527 --> 01:55:46.271
"My life changed because of that."

3336
01:55:46.271 --> 01:55:47.940
That means something to me.

3337
01:55:47.940 --> 01:55:50.780
And I don't know if that's a selfish thing or an ego thing,

3338
01:55:50.780 --> 01:55:55.160
but that's how I conduct myself.

3339
01:55:55.160 --> 01:55:58.300
Whereas in my 20's,

3340
01:55:58.300 --> 01:56:00.130
it was more about,

3341
01:56:00.130 --> 01:56:02.520
I'm the new Tiger Woods of the vegan bodybuilding world.

3342
01:56:02.520 --> 01:56:06.220
I'm the best thing that's come to this movement

3343
01:56:06.220 --> 01:56:07.053
kind of thing.
You got driven

3344
01:56:07.053 --> 01:56:07.886
versus mission driven.

3345
01:56:07.886 --> 01:56:10.323
Yeah, but that was also the time.

3346
01:56:10.323 --> 01:56:12.550
I was in my 20's.

3347
01:56:12.550 --> 01:56:14.260
I think we've all gone through some of these phases,

3348
01:56:14.260 --> 01:56:16.210
where I wanted the magazine covers,

3349
01:56:16.210 --> 01:56:17.450
I wanted the TV stuff,

3350
01:56:17.450 --> 01:56:18.560
I wanted the newspapers,

3351
01:56:18.560 --> 01:56:20.033
I wanted the microphone.

3352
01:56:21.189 --> 01:56:25.250
And now I realize that there's so many messengers out there.

3353
01:56:25.250 --> 01:56:29.370
And so, elevating all of these other athletes

3354
01:56:29.370 --> 01:56:31.010
who are just in many cases,

3355
01:56:31.010 --> 01:56:33.570
better representatives as athletes.

3356
01:56:33.570 --> 01:56:34.890
They perform better in their sport.

3357
01:56:34.890 --> 01:56:36.183
They have better results.

3358
01:56:37.295 --> 01:56:39.120
Whether they have a smaller audience or bigger audience,

3359
01:56:39.120 --> 01:56:43.320
but just giving them an amplified platform

3360
01:56:43.320 --> 01:56:45.710
to just showcase what they're doing

3361
01:56:45.710 --> 01:56:47.520
is something that really means a lot to me now

3362
01:56:47.520 --> 01:56:48.930
in my advocacy.

3363
01:56:48.930 --> 01:56:50.080
I've never been one.

3364
01:56:50.080 --> 01:56:52.130
I've participated in protests and stuff,

3365
01:56:52.130 --> 01:56:53.130
but I'm not good at it.

3366
01:56:53.130 --> 01:56:54.220
This is not my personality.

3367
01:56:54.220 --> 01:56:56.660
Confrontational stuff is...

3368
01:56:56.660 --> 01:56:59.455
I know some people, I wish I were more like that,

3369
01:56:59.455 --> 01:57:00.600
including my wife,

3370
01:57:00.600 --> 01:57:02.530
I wish I was just more assertive in those kinds of things,

3371
01:57:02.530 --> 01:57:04.000
but I'm just not.

3372
01:57:04.000 --> 01:57:07.640
I'm not and I'm much more of what can I do?

3373
01:57:07.640 --> 01:57:10.720
What's the best use of my time to create the most change?

3374
01:57:10.720 --> 01:57:12.470
And that's where writing came from.

3375
01:57:14.590 --> 01:57:16.440
That's why I wanted a book like this.

3376
01:57:17.546 --> 01:57:20.380
It took a lot of manifesting, so to speak,

3377
01:57:20.380 --> 01:57:21.930
to get a hard cover book like this.

3378
01:57:21.930 --> 01:57:23.380
To self published books for a decade

3379
01:57:23.380 --> 01:57:25.640
and be on this pursuit since I was in third grade

3380
01:57:25.640 --> 01:57:27.640
and said someday I'm gonna be an author.

3381
01:57:28.810 --> 01:57:30.190
That's a platform for me.

3382
01:57:30.190 --> 01:57:32.370
I think I'm a better writer than I am a speaker.

3383
01:57:32.370 --> 01:57:34.190
I'm better at that than I am

3384
01:57:34.190 --> 01:57:35.900
at talking about animal rights.

3385
01:57:35.900 --> 01:57:37.700
Even if I feel it inside,

3386
01:57:37.700 --> 01:57:39.610
I'm not as great as a communicator,

3387
01:57:39.610 --> 01:57:41.290
as others who can just articulate

3388
01:57:41.290 --> 01:57:42.123
their thoughts and feelings better.

3389
01:57:42.123 --> 01:57:44.480
Right, I do watch those Earthling Ed videos

3390
01:57:44.480 --> 01:57:46.500
and it looks like he just naturally

3391
01:57:46.500 --> 01:57:48.230
is able to just pontificate

3392
01:57:48.230 --> 01:57:51.280
in the most eloquent way on these issues.

3393
01:57:51.280 --> 01:57:52.593
Yeah, and there's Joey Carbstrong

3394
01:57:52.593 --> 01:57:54.233
and plenty of other people.

3395
01:57:55.240 --> 01:57:57.120
That's their strength.

3396
01:57:57.120 --> 01:57:59.733
And so, what I've tried to use as my experience,

3397
01:58:00.740 --> 01:58:02.320
how many people have been a plant-based athlete

3398
01:58:02.320 --> 01:58:03.380
for a quarter century

3399
01:58:03.380 --> 01:58:06.470
and along that journey have gained 100 pounds

3400
01:58:06.470 --> 01:58:09.440
and have been able to have all these different experiences,

3401
01:58:09.440 --> 01:58:10.810
'cause that's one of the arguments

3402
01:58:10.810 --> 01:58:11.850
against the plant-based diet.

3403
01:58:11.850 --> 01:58:13.840
Oh, you'll do it for a year or two and then you'll fail

