3662
02:07:49.240 --> 02:07:53.760
How does that work from a nutritional standpoint?

3663
02:07:53.760 --> 02:07:55.670
And I'd like to see some of that.

3664
02:07:55.670 --> 02:07:56.823
So, you went to him and asked him that?

3665
02:07:56.823 --> 02:07:57.883
What did he say?

3666
02:07:59.690 --> 02:08:00.730
There's no study.

3667
02:08:00.730 --> 02:08:02.080
He's all about data and research.

3668
02:08:02.080 --> 02:08:03.034
Well, we don't know.

3669
02:08:03.034 --> 02:08:03.867
Right.

3670
02:08:03.867 --> 02:08:04.700
We don't know.

3671
02:08:04.700 --> 02:08:05.670
And I (chuckles) even said, 'cause I don't know--

3672
02:08:05.670 --> 02:08:08.060
Well, Garth Davis would be another candidate.

3673
02:08:08.060 --> 02:08:09.490
Well, he's not a research scientist,

3674
02:08:09.490 --> 02:08:12.720
but somebody who could perhaps spearhead

3675
02:08:12.720 --> 02:08:15.310
or create a situation

3676
02:08:15.310 --> 02:08:18.200
in which a study like that could be conducted.

3677
02:08:18.200 --> 02:08:19.033
I was even saying,

3678
02:08:19.033 --> 02:08:20.460
because I don't know how a lot of this stuff works,

3679
02:08:20.460 --> 02:08:22.450
the actual scientific study.

3680
02:08:22.450 --> 02:08:24.859
I said, "Can we do something here, Dr. Campbell?"

3681
02:08:24.859 --> 02:08:25.692
(laughs)

3682
02:08:25.692 --> 02:08:26.525
He's enthusiastic.

3683
02:08:26.525 --> 02:08:28.930
He obviously has endorsed really all of my work

3684
02:08:28.930 --> 02:08:31.160
and he knows that I came to this conclusion

3685
02:08:31.160 --> 02:08:34.360
based on his program from the Center for Nutrition Studies.

3686
02:08:34.360 --> 02:08:36.760
He knows why I adopted a low protein diet

3687
02:08:36.760 --> 02:08:40.380
or what we can call an adequate protein diet, I guess.

3688
02:08:40.380 --> 02:08:42.950
But I would love to participate in something

3689
02:08:42.950 --> 02:08:44.313
if it were available, but I don't know.

3690
02:08:44.313 --> 02:08:49.000
And I don't know how many people are willing to do that.

3691
02:08:49.000 --> 02:08:50.970
So, basically, the way you would style it

3692
02:08:50.970 --> 02:08:53.030
is you'd get a group of people

3693
02:08:53.030 --> 02:08:55.150
and you'd put them in the gym.

3694
02:08:55.150 --> 02:08:56.170
You'd separate them.

3695
02:08:56.170 --> 02:08:58.340
You'd put them on strict diets.

3696
02:08:58.340 --> 02:09:00.800
One with a higher protein

3697
02:09:00.800 --> 02:09:03.070
and the other on more of your protocol,

3698
02:09:03.070 --> 02:09:06.820
and then just calibrate their gains over a 30 day period

3699
02:09:06.820 --> 02:09:08.403
or something like that, right?

3700
02:09:08.403 --> 02:09:09.280
You'd have to control--

3701
02:09:09.280 --> 02:09:10.620
I think that kind of thing has happened somewhere, right,

3702
02:09:10.620 --> 02:09:11.750
with the plant protein

3703
02:09:11.750 --> 02:09:14.020
versus animal protein studies of people.

3704
02:09:14.020 --> 02:09:15.580
Right, but it's always unclear

3705
02:09:15.580 --> 02:09:17.243
what exactly did these people eat?

3706
02:09:17.243 --> 02:09:18.945
Yeah, that's true.

3707
02:09:18.945 --> 02:09:19.778
Controlling the variables is--

3708
02:09:19.778 --> 02:09:21.690
And they're also going for that threshold

3709
02:09:21.690 --> 02:09:26.690
of we wanna maximize the 1.6 grams of protein per kilogram,

3710
02:09:27.290 --> 02:09:28.800
for true muscle building.

3711
02:09:28.800 --> 02:09:31.640
And so, it's still on the higher end of protein intake,

3712
02:09:31.640 --> 02:09:33.220
even if it's plant versus animal protein,

3713
02:09:33.220 --> 02:09:37.770
including the most recent study we referenced in the book.

3714
02:09:37.770 --> 02:09:38.650
So, that's what I'm saying.

3715
02:09:38.650 --> 02:09:40.800
I'd like to see on the lower protein side

3716
02:09:40.800 --> 02:09:42.066
and just see how it works.

3717
02:09:42.066 --> 02:09:44.330
The calories can be the same,

3718
02:09:44.330 --> 02:09:46.270
but get more complex carbohydrates in there,

3719
02:09:46.270 --> 02:09:47.570
or a few more fats in there

3720
02:09:47.570 --> 02:09:49.750
from these really nutrient dense sources

3721
02:09:49.750 --> 02:09:52.250
and let's see what the real difference is,

3722
02:09:52.250 --> 02:09:54.930
because I feel like it's something I experienced for myself.

3723
02:09:54.930 --> 02:09:56.290
I talked to Niemeyer about it,

3724
02:09:56.290 --> 02:09:59.120
and he was intrigued and started to apply some of that

3725
02:09:59.120 --> 02:10:00.520
for himself as well.

3726
02:10:00.520 --> 02:10:03.818
And I feel like maybe that could be the next frontier

3727
02:10:03.818 --> 02:10:06.810
in plant-based athleticism,

3728
02:10:06.810 --> 02:10:09.070
just shifting our focus more

3729
02:10:09.070 --> 02:10:12.300
on complex carbohydrates versus protein obsession.

3730
02:10:12.300 --> 02:10:13.441
Yeah.

3731
02:10:13.441 --> 02:10:14.274
Do you think that's what it'll take, though,

3732
02:10:14.274 --> 02:10:15.107
for the mainstream athletes

3733
02:10:15.107 --> 02:10:16.640
to really adopt this,

3734
02:10:16.640 --> 02:10:19.410
where it's like that's now the standard diet,

3735
02:10:19.410 --> 02:10:21.580
or do you think it's just gonna take one superstar

3736
02:10:21.580 --> 02:10:22.550
and someone's gonna follow it

3737
02:10:22.550 --> 02:10:24.650
and then suddenly it will be the booming thing?

3738
02:10:24.650 --> 02:10:27.210
It's like that whole industry versus academia thing.

3739
02:10:27.210 --> 02:10:28.890
Maybe in theory, this is gonna be better,

3740
02:10:28.890 --> 02:10:31.734
but until we see that everyone's doing it,

3741
02:10:31.734 --> 02:10:33.150
because it's the gold standard now for nutrition

3742
02:10:33.150 --> 02:10:33.983
and it's the way

3743
02:10:33.983 --> 02:10:36.060
to get paid the most, honestly, in your sports

3744
02:10:36.060 --> 02:10:37.373
on this mainstream level.

3745
02:10:38.460 --> 02:10:39.400
I don't know.

3746
02:10:39.400 --> 02:10:41.130
But we're seeing so many

3747
02:10:41.130 --> 02:10:42.980
begin to be sprinkled in all the different sports

3748
02:10:42.980 --> 02:10:43.813
that are doing that.

3749
02:10:43.813 --> 02:10:46.010
I think that's not far off from happening.

3750
02:10:46.010 --> 02:10:47.270
Yeah, I think it's both.

3751
02:10:47.270 --> 02:10:48.120
I think that's a great question.

3752
02:10:48.120 --> 02:10:52.860
I think it's a bottom-up and top-down situation, right?

3753
02:10:52.860 --> 02:10:55.179
From, the bottom up perspective,

3754
02:10:55.179 --> 02:10:59.660
you need this groundswell movement of people

3755
02:10:59.660 --> 02:11:01.687
who are inspired by the books

3756
02:11:01.687 --> 02:11:04.310
and the YouTube videos and the podcasts

3757
02:11:04.310 --> 02:11:06.610
to give it a try in their own daily lives

3758
02:11:06.610 --> 02:11:09.280
and then you need the superstar athlete

3759
02:11:09.280 --> 02:11:11.750
who ends up doing it and crushes it

3760
02:11:11.750 --> 02:11:16.750
in a way that defies all the kind of poo-poos who say,

3761
02:11:18.897 --> 02:11:21.160
"Oh, well that person's a freak of nature,"

3762
02:11:21.160 --> 02:11:24.090
or "It's a one-off," or "This is an outlier,"

3763
02:11:24.090 --> 02:11:26.860
or "They were already great before."

3764
02:11:26.860 --> 02:11:29.090
You're gonna need a critical mass

3765
02:11:29.090 --> 02:11:31.630
of really elite, high performance athletes

3766
02:11:31.630 --> 02:11:35.230
across a diversity of sports, I think,

3767
02:11:35.230 --> 02:11:39.200
before you get to a cultural tipping point.

3768
02:11:39.200 --> 02:11:41.230
We're moving towards that,

3769
02:11:41.230 --> 02:11:44.830
but right now when you canvas like professional sports

3770
02:11:44.830 --> 02:11:46.850
and you have a bunch of these people in the book,

3771
02:11:46.850 --> 02:11:49.930
but we haven't reached critical mass if we're being honest.

3772
02:11:49.930 --> 02:11:51.753
There's a couple people here and there.

3773
02:11:51.753 --> 02:11:52.586
(laughs)

3774
02:11:52.586 --> 02:11:53.720
And to be fair,

3775
02:11:53.720 --> 02:11:54.730
it's a lot to ask

3776
02:11:54.730 --> 02:11:57.470
if you're getting paid millions of dollars a year

3777
02:11:57.470 --> 02:12:01.860
and your entire life is premised upon you performing

3778
02:12:01.860 --> 02:12:05.670
at the highest level in your given sport

3779
02:12:05.670 --> 02:12:07.390
to say, hey, I want you to throw out

3780
02:12:07.390 --> 02:12:08.980
everything you ever thought you knew about nutrition

3781
02:12:08.980 --> 02:12:10.640
and try this other thing.

3782
02:12:10.640 --> 02:12:13.440
The risk analysis doesn't make sense

3783
02:12:13.440 --> 02:12:15.490
for that person to roll the dice

3784
02:12:15.490 --> 02:12:18.900
until there's enough people that create that critical mass

3785
02:12:18.900 --> 02:12:20.820
and a feeling of security

3786
02:12:20.820 --> 02:12:24.350
in starting to segue into that direction.

3787
02:12:24.350 --> 02:12:26.580
And that may never happen.

3788
02:12:26.580 --> 02:12:28.252
I'm kind of glad we came back to this

3789
02:12:28.252 --> 02:12:29.800
and that you mentioned not overstating the point in there

3790
02:12:29.800 --> 02:12:31.380
because I only realized just this past week

3791
02:12:31.380 --> 02:12:33.940
as I was reading the book more and thinking more about it,

3792
02:12:33.940 --> 02:12:36.300
that this isn't really about,

3793
02:12:36.300 --> 02:12:38.990
at least, I don't think for me or Robert,

3794
02:12:38.990 --> 02:12:41.313
it's not about convincing top athletes

3795
02:12:41.313 --> 02:12:43.860
that this is the way to get better at your sport,

3796
02:12:43.860 --> 02:12:45.990
because we don't know that.

3797
02:12:45.990 --> 02:12:48.130
I think the hypothesis here, the premise

3798
02:12:48.130 --> 02:12:51.853
is that this is a viable alternative to the other diets now.

3799
02:12:52.804 --> 02:12:54.680
Maybe the steady state we're gonna reach

3800
02:12:54.680 --> 02:12:57.460
is that in pro sports, there's the paleo, the keto,

3801
02:12:57.460 --> 02:12:58.702
I don't know about keto,

3802
02:12:58.702 --> 02:12:59.535
(chuckles)

3803
02:12:59.535 --> 02:13:02.225
but there's the paleo, there's the vegans or plant-based

3804
02:13:02.225 --> 02:13:03.420
and it's not that one dominates

3805
02:13:03.420 --> 02:13:04.910
because maybe all these work

3806
02:13:04.910 --> 02:13:07.270
for short-term sports performance,

3807
02:13:07.270 --> 02:13:09.800
short-term meaning 5, 10, 15 years.

3808
02:13:09.800 --> 02:13:11.850
I think this one, the plant-based one,

3809
02:13:11.850 --> 02:13:13.420
is the one that's gonna make those people

3810
02:13:13.420 --> 02:13:14.930
way happier and healthier

3811
02:13:14.930 --> 02:13:16.855
after their careers are over.

3812
02:13:16.855 --> 02:13:17.688
But I don't know.

3813
02:13:17.688 --> 02:13:19.287
But I wonder if that's okay.

3814
02:13:19.287 --> 02:13:21.840
No, I would state it a little bit more

3815
02:13:23.010 --> 02:13:24.480
stridently than that

3816
02:13:25.630 --> 02:13:30.630
to say that not only is it a viable alternative,

3817
02:13:31.520 --> 02:13:34.640
I think there are advantages to it

3818
02:13:34.640 --> 02:13:36.390
that outweigh other protocols,

3819
02:13:36.390 --> 02:13:38.930
particularly for athletes

3820
02:13:38.930 --> 02:13:41.040
who are approaching the twilight of their career.

3821
02:13:41.040 --> 02:13:42.580
When you look at Tom Brady,

3822
02:13:42.580 --> 02:13:44.700
now, Tom Brady is never gonna say

3823
02:13:44.700 --> 02:13:47.160
that he's a plant-based athlete or that he's a vegan

3824
02:13:47.160 --> 02:13:49.990
and he's not, technically,

3825
02:13:49.990 --> 02:13:53.513
but the guy eats a very plant forward diet

3826
02:13:53.513 --> 02:13:54.730
for the most part.

3827
02:13:54.730 --> 02:13:56.380
There's some animal products in there,

3828
02:13:56.380 --> 02:14:01.380
but the guy's essentially eating a "plant-based diet."

3829
02:14:01.440 --> 02:14:03.210
He's crushing it in a way

3830
02:14:03.210 --> 02:14:06.760
that no other athlete in his position ever has.

3831
02:14:06.760 --> 02:14:08.200
People are paying attention.

3832
02:14:08.200 --> 02:14:10.190
He gets made fun of for it at the same time,

3833
02:14:10.190 --> 02:14:13.093
but you cannot deny the incredible results

3834
02:14:13.093 --> 02:14:14.920
that this guy's getting.

3835
02:14:14.920 --> 02:14:18.370
So, when you're in that twilight space

3836
02:14:18.370 --> 02:14:20.240
and you're starting to get injured more

3837
02:14:20.240 --> 02:14:21.880
and you just can't get out of bed

3838
02:14:21.880 --> 02:14:23.520
in the way that you used to,

3839
02:14:23.520 --> 02:14:26.900
I think there's a receptivity to this way of eating.

3840
02:14:26.900 --> 02:14:31.160
Those people are suddenly looking for that extra edge

3841
02:14:31.160 --> 02:14:35.650
and a way to extend their career another season or two.

3842
02:14:35.650 --> 02:14:37.050
And I think those are the people

3843
02:14:37.050 --> 02:14:40.340
that are the ones who are jumping on board here

3844
02:14:40.340 --> 02:14:42.347
and I think it builds from there.

3845
02:14:42.347 --> 02:14:44.190
And you know who embodies that

3846
02:14:44.190 --> 02:14:46.230
more than anyone to me right now

3847
02:14:46.230 --> 02:14:47.690
is Chris Paul.

3848
02:14:47.690 --> 02:14:48.523
Chris Paul--

3849
02:14:48.523 --> 02:14:49.356
Right, that's a good point.

3850
02:14:49.356 --> 02:14:50.540
I just had a chance to just meet him briefly,

3851
02:14:50.540 --> 02:14:51.760
talk briefly with him in person

3852
02:14:51.760 --> 02:14:54.660
but he said those exact things.

3853
02:14:54.660 --> 02:14:55.760
You look at his quotes

3854
02:14:55.760 --> 02:14:57.290
and he talked about

3855
02:14:57.290 --> 02:14:58.690
how he adopted a plant-based diet

3856
02:14:58.690 --> 02:15:00.180
and within a short amount of time,

3857
02:15:00.180 --> 02:15:01.410
a couple of months into it,

3858
02:15:01.410 --> 02:15:03.190
where's the pain and stiffness

3859
02:15:03.190 --> 02:15:05.720
I used to have in the morning when you would wake up?

3860
02:15:05.720 --> 02:15:07.510
And you look at his career,

3861
02:15:07.510 --> 02:15:09.260
he was an amazing player

3862
02:15:09.260 --> 02:15:11.260
and then was off the All-Star team

3863
02:15:11.260 --> 02:15:13.170
for two or three seasons in a row,

3864
02:15:13.170 --> 02:15:17.160
adopted a plant-based diet, talks about it enthusiastically,

3865
02:15:17.160 --> 02:15:20.350
returned as an All-Star every season since,

3866
02:15:20.350 --> 02:15:23.050
every team he's got on has gotten better.

3867
02:15:23.050 --> 02:15:25.230
He's nearly an MVP candidate this year.

3868
02:15:25.230 --> 02:15:26.676
He's probably in the top 10.

3869
02:15:26.676 --> 02:15:30.350
And he talks about this renaissance career

3870
02:15:30.350 --> 02:15:31.525
that he's having.

3871
02:15:31.525 --> 02:15:33.610
He brought his athleticism back.

3872
02:15:33.610 --> 02:15:34.690
He got his first dunk.

3873
02:15:34.690 --> 02:15:36.970
It sounds silly, but he's a smaller guy,

3874
02:15:36.970 --> 02:15:39.270
maybe a little bit taller than me.

3875
02:15:39.270 --> 02:15:40.960
He got his first dunk ever in a game.

3876
02:15:40.960 --> 02:15:43.630
It was this two-handed alley-oop dunk from Russell Westbrook

3877
02:15:43.630 --> 02:15:44.463
in the All-Star game.

3878
02:15:44.463 --> 02:15:45.296
It was awesome.

3879
02:15:45.296 --> 02:15:46.460
It was a highlight for me.

3880
02:15:46.460 --> 02:15:47.924
One more proof do we need, right?

3881
02:15:47.924 --> 02:15:48.757
(laughs)

3882
02:15:48.757 --> 02:15:53.220
But really he's a prominent NBA basketball player.

3883
02:15:53.220 --> 02:15:55.770
And the fact that JaVale McGee met him briefly also

3884
02:15:55.770 --> 02:15:58.120
and won a championship last year.

3885
02:15:58.120 --> 02:16:00.610
Won as a major player on the Lakers

3886
02:16:00.610 --> 02:16:02.930
and has been plant-based for years now.

3887
02:16:02.930 --> 02:16:03.880
and DeAndre Jordan.

3888
02:16:03.880 --> 02:16:04.880
And there was a time

3889
02:16:05.910 --> 02:16:07.220
in one of the early editions of this book,

3890
02:16:07.220 --> 02:16:09.990
where one third of the entire Brooklyn Nets team

3891
02:16:09.990 --> 02:16:11.180
was plant-based.

3892
02:16:11.180 --> 02:16:12.520
Now some of those guys got traded.

3893
02:16:12.520 --> 02:16:13.860
Wilson Chandler's no longer there,

3894
02:16:13.860 --> 02:16:15.540
Garrett Temple is no longer there,

3895
02:16:15.540 --> 02:16:18.100
Kyrie I hope is still 100%

3896
02:16:18.100 --> 02:16:22.130
although I'm not quite sure he's 100% vegan now.

3897
02:16:22.130 --> 02:16:24.370
The Redskins had a thing going on for a while, too.

3898
02:16:24.370 --> 02:16:25.650
They did, 2017

3899
02:16:25.650 --> 02:16:30.330
and the Titans did around the same time, 2017, as well

3900
02:16:30.330 --> 02:16:31.600
with Derek Morgan

3901
02:16:31.600 --> 02:16:36.030
and, of course, Erin Foster and early Tony Gonzalez.

3902
02:16:36.030 --> 02:16:37.960
Yeah, Erin Foster he's retired,

3903
02:16:37.960 --> 02:16:41.300
but also he kind of moved away from it.

3904
02:16:41.300 --> 02:16:43.480
But he did it exclusively for what a while.

3905
02:16:43.480 --> 02:16:45.780
He was in touch with Forks Over Knives on a regular basis

3906
02:16:45.780 --> 02:16:49.150
and he was the number one running back that season

3907
02:16:49.150 --> 02:16:50.810
in numerous categories,

3908
02:16:50.810 --> 02:16:53.710
including rushing attempts and touchdowns,

3909
02:16:53.710 --> 02:16:54.710
something like that.

3910
02:16:56.750 --> 02:16:59.870
Chris Paul is a great example of these twilight years.

3911
02:16:59.870 --> 02:17:03.500
He's playing his best basketball ever later in his career.

3912
02:17:03.500 --> 02:17:06.860
Serena Williams is another one who's just dominant.

3913
02:17:06.860 --> 02:17:11.040
Zdeno Chara in the place with the Bruins he's crushing it.

3914
02:17:11.040 --> 02:17:12.680
I don't actually know it.

3915
02:17:12.680 --> 02:17:14.930
Yeah, you gotta get on this guy.

3916
02:17:14.930 --> 02:17:18.080
I think I heard about him from the Game Changers.

3917
02:17:18.080 --> 02:17:19.803
I followed them on Instagram, but just--

3918
02:17:19.803 --> 02:17:20.860
He's killing it.

3919
02:17:20.860 --> 02:17:23.370
There's so many athletes out there now doing it.

3920
02:17:23.370 --> 02:17:24.940
Messi during the season.

3921
02:17:24.940 --> 02:17:26.540
Lionel Messi is apparently vegan.

3922
02:17:26.540 --> 02:17:27.373
I haven't confirmed this

3923
02:17:27.373 --> 02:17:28.477
but that's what appears to be.

3924
02:17:28.477 --> 02:17:30.840
And he's kind of on the down slope of his career.

3925
02:17:30.840 --> 02:17:31.673
So, it's great but--

3926
02:17:31.673 --> 02:17:32.520
Lewis Hamilton.

3927
02:17:32.520 --> 02:17:34.638
Alex Morgan, Novak Djokovich.

3928
02:17:34.638 --> 02:17:36.719
There's a lot there.

3929
02:17:36.719 --> 02:17:38.080
There's a lot of great athletes.

3930
02:17:38.080 --> 02:17:39.620
We mentioned a bunch of them

3931
02:17:39.620 --> 02:17:41.830
and even some who maybe are not doing it now,

3932
02:17:41.830 --> 02:17:45.180
like Mike Tyson but, again, I talk with him in person.

3933
02:17:45.180 --> 02:17:47.130
He was doing it for years

3934
02:17:47.130 --> 02:17:49.930
and he got so many benefits from it.

3935
02:17:49.930 --> 02:17:52.180
He lost a whole bunch of weight and felt all this stuff

3936
02:17:52.180 --> 02:17:54.200
and then I think he kind of crept back into

3937
02:17:54.200 --> 02:17:55.883
now making my comeback,

3938
02:17:57.100 --> 02:17:58.370
fighting for millions of dollars,

3939
02:17:58.370 --> 02:18:00.170
basically, for charity now

3940
02:18:00.170 --> 02:18:02.430
and he went back to some of that desire

3941
02:18:02.430 --> 02:18:04.140
for animal protein or something,

3942
02:18:04.140 --> 02:18:06.170
but he was in vegan campaigns for years

3943
02:18:06.170 --> 02:18:08.720
and he credits a lot of that

3944
02:18:08.720 --> 02:18:12.440
to his health resurgence from a plant-based diet

3945
02:18:12.440 --> 02:18:14.120
and many elite athletes have

3946
02:18:14.120 --> 02:18:14.953
and we're hoping,

3947
02:18:14.953 --> 02:18:17.110
yeah, we're certainly not there.

3948
02:18:17.110 --> 02:18:19.710
We're not at some sort of tipping point or critical mass.

3949
02:18:19.710 --> 02:18:21.930
We wish we had more names to add in this book.

3950
02:18:21.930 --> 02:18:26.750
Sure. But I think if you go back 15 years

3951
02:18:26.750 --> 02:18:28.943
and had to guess where the culture would be

3952
02:18:28.943 --> 02:18:30.930
and now where it is right now,

3953
02:18:30.930 --> 02:18:34.420
I think we've exceeded any expectation that any of us had

3954
02:18:34.420 --> 02:18:35.598
in terms of adoption.

3955
02:18:35.598 --> 02:18:37.596
Absolutely, no question about it.

3956
02:18:37.596 --> 02:18:38.429
Yep.

3957
02:18:38.429 --> 02:18:42.110
I wanna round this out with one last thread,

3958
02:18:42.110 --> 02:18:44.840
which is another thing you talk about in the book

3959
02:18:44.840 --> 02:18:46.337
and I think it's really important

3960
02:18:46.337 --> 02:18:50.270
and something that I know

3961
02:18:50.270 --> 02:18:53.000
a lot of people who are playing around with

3962
02:18:53.000 --> 02:18:54.370
this lifestyle contend with,

3963
02:18:54.370 --> 02:18:57.947
which is dealing with an unreceptive,

3964
02:18:57.947 --> 02:18:59.410
(chuckles) social circle.

3965
02:18:59.410 --> 02:19:01.980
We talked about it in the context of your kids

3966
02:19:01.980 --> 02:19:03.900
but a lot of people,

3967
02:19:03.900 --> 02:19:06.490
I think we underestimate the impact

3968
02:19:06.490 --> 02:19:10.720
of just navigating people in our lives,

3969
02:19:10.720 --> 02:19:12.270
in terms of the impact that that has

3970
02:19:12.270 --> 02:19:14.640
on the lifestyle choices that we make.

3971
02:19:14.640 --> 02:19:16.010
Just look, it's healthy, just do it.

3972
02:19:16.010 --> 02:19:18.230
But then when you're at the dinner party

3973
02:19:18.230 --> 02:19:19.590
or you gotta go do this thing,

3974
02:19:19.590 --> 02:19:23.170
it's just easier to go along to get along

3975
02:19:23.170 --> 02:19:24.647
and it's harder to say,

3976
02:19:24.647 --> 02:19:26.290
"No, I'm doing this for myself

3977
02:19:26.290 --> 02:19:28.797
and I'm carving out and this is who I am."

3978
02:19:30.050 --> 02:19:32.010
So, you mean standing up for yourself,

3979
02:19:32.010 --> 02:19:34.160
not trying to push it on--

3980
02:19:34.160 --> 02:19:39.160
Right, how do you kind of remain true to your own values

3981
02:19:40.070 --> 02:19:45.070
and also manage the naysayers in your life

3982
02:19:45.230 --> 02:19:47.150
or the people that are kind of trying to talk you

3983
02:19:47.150 --> 02:19:48.220
out of doing this thing

3984
02:19:48.220 --> 02:19:50.073
that you wanna explore for yourself?

3985
02:19:50.910 --> 02:19:54.430
I think it depends so much on the person, of course.

3986
02:19:54.430 --> 02:19:57.660
For me, if I was going to a dinner party,

3987
02:19:57.660 --> 02:19:58.790
the last thing on my mind

3988
02:19:58.790 --> 02:19:59.623
would be the idea

3989
02:19:59.623 --> 02:20:02.360
that maybe I could convert someone here into this.

3990
02:20:02.360 --> 02:20:03.240
Yeah, no, I'm not talking about that.

3991
02:20:03.240 --> 02:20:05.500
I'm just talking about feeling comfortable

3992
02:20:05.500 --> 02:20:06.333
in your own skin.

3993
02:20:06.333 --> 02:20:08.154
Sure, but I'm only making the point

3994
02:20:08.154 --> 02:20:09.130
that that's where I started

3995
02:20:09.130 --> 02:20:10.660
with saying, I'm not gonna be doing that,

3996
02:20:10.660 --> 02:20:12.243
'cause some people do say as soon as they go vegan

3997
02:20:12.243 --> 02:20:13.440
that they wanna tell everyone

3998
02:20:13.440 --> 02:20:15.900
and show their family or whatever

3999
02:20:15.900 --> 02:20:18.190
that they also shall do this.

4000
02:20:18.190 --> 02:20:21.100
Just life tip that doesn't work out--

4001
02:20:21.100 --> 02:20:21.933
No, it doesn't,

4002
02:20:21.933 --> 02:20:22.766
but people still think

4003
02:20:22.766 --> 02:20:23.700
it's right.
Stop doing that.

4004
02:20:23.700 --> 02:20:26.483
Right, so, I started there.

4005
02:20:27.450 --> 02:20:30.410
Like everything else, openness.

4006
02:20:30.410 --> 02:20:31.877
Don't show up at the party and say,

4007
02:20:31.877 --> 02:20:32.710
"Hey, by the way,

4008
02:20:32.710 --> 02:20:34.070
"I'm trying to eat this plant-based diet.

4009
02:20:34.070 --> 02:20:36.290
"I'm not gonna eat what you're making,"

4010
02:20:36.290 --> 02:20:38.220
but communicating in advance, obviously,

4011
02:20:38.220 --> 02:20:39.363
eating ahead of time,

4012
02:20:40.440 --> 02:20:43.470
which I think is kind of common sense,

4013
02:20:43.470 --> 02:20:46.280
but I just never expected anyone to cater to me.

4014
02:20:46.280 --> 02:20:47.327
I was never gonna show up and say,

4015
02:20:47.327 --> 02:20:48.527
"Hey, this is what I'm doing now.

4016
02:20:48.527 --> 02:20:50.650
"I expect that there was gonna be this stuff there for me."

4017
02:20:50.650 --> 02:20:51.648
You need to re-align

4018
02:20:51.648 --> 02:20:53.214
everything you're doing to meet my...

4019
02:20:53.214 --> 02:20:54.133
(laughs)

4020
02:20:54.133 --> 02:20:58.060
And so, that combined with a healthy amount

4021
02:20:58.060 --> 02:21:00.800
of being willing to laugh at it,

4022
02:21:00.800 --> 02:21:03.380
'cause my uncle would at one point,

4023
02:21:03.380 --> 02:21:05.470
pretty early in me being vegetarian,

4024
02:21:05.470 --> 02:21:07.120
not yet vegan, I don't think,

4025
02:21:07.120 --> 02:21:08.717
at a big 4th of July thing,

4026
02:21:08.717 --> 02:21:09.550
the whole family was there.

4027
02:21:09.550 --> 02:21:11.470
There was probably 30 people there.

4028
02:21:11.470 --> 02:21:13.540
And he brought out some lettuce on a plate.

4029
02:21:13.540 --> 02:21:14.450
Everyone's was eating crabs

4030
02:21:14.450 --> 02:21:15.454
and he said,

4031
02:21:15.454 --> 02:21:16.287
"Hey Matt,

4032
02:21:16.287 --> 02:21:17.120
"here's your dinner."
"This is for you, Matt."

4033
02:21:17.120 --> 02:21:17.953
Yeah, of course.

4034
02:21:17.953 --> 02:21:19.320
And, I guess, a different person might get upset

4035
02:21:19.320 --> 02:21:21.880
and make it a big scene or something but I just laughed.

4036
02:21:21.880 --> 02:21:23.020
I don't know what else to do.

4037
02:21:23.020 --> 02:21:25.207
I'm not gonna win that situation, I don't think

4038
02:21:25.207 --> 02:21:26.267
and I personally think,

4039
02:21:26.267 --> 02:21:28.010
and I know people disagree with me on this,

4040
02:21:28.010 --> 02:21:30.554
but I think by laughing there,

4041
02:21:30.554 --> 02:21:32.360
you really kinda break the pattern

4042
02:21:32.360 --> 02:21:34.320
of someone expecting you to get offended

4043
02:21:34.320 --> 02:21:35.380
and expecting that their joke's

4044
02:21:35.380 --> 02:21:37.300
gonna really have a big impact on you.

4045
02:21:37.300 --> 02:21:39.040
And if instead you can also kind of laugh

4046
02:21:39.040 --> 02:21:42.105
or like make some other joke that just goes to their level--

4047
02:21:42.105 --> 02:21:43.383
I would just double down.

4048
02:21:44.390 --> 02:21:47.020
Go way overboard in terms of how happy you are

4049
02:21:47.020 --> 02:21:48.010
that he went out of his way

4050
02:21:48.010 --> 02:21:49.414
to give you the piece of lettuce.

4051
02:21:49.414 --> 02:21:50.247
(chuckles)

4052
02:21:50.247 --> 02:21:51.830
Yeah, and I think that disarms people.

4053
02:21:51.830 --> 02:21:52.663
I think that makes them say,

4054
02:21:52.663 --> 02:21:53.496
"Hey, wait a minute.

4055
02:21:53.496 --> 02:21:55.777
"Maybe not all of them are these militant people

4056
02:21:55.777 --> 02:21:57.743
"who are out to change."

4057
02:21:57.743 --> 02:21:58.966
And then, of course,

4058
02:21:58.966 --> 02:22:01.870
if you're also happening to drop 30 pounds

4059
02:22:01.870 --> 02:22:04.703
or happening to start training for a half marathon,

4060
02:22:05.610 --> 02:22:07.440
whether or not that's actually what your diet

4061
02:22:07.440 --> 02:22:08.490
has caused you to do,

4062
02:22:08.490 --> 02:22:10.420
but if it's just that's your method of saying,

4063
02:22:10.420 --> 02:22:11.340
hey, I'm gonna demonstrate

4064
02:22:11.340 --> 02:22:13.193
that this is a good way to eat

4065
02:22:13.193 --> 02:22:14.610
or that this is working for me.

4066
02:22:14.610 --> 02:22:15.870
I'm gonna do this,

4067
02:22:15.870 --> 02:22:16.703
even if it's, like I said,

4068
02:22:16.703 --> 02:22:20.380
if it's unrelated to the effect your diet is having on you,

4069
02:22:20.380 --> 02:22:21.510
I think, again, it just comes back

4070
02:22:21.510 --> 02:22:22.343
to that being an example thing

4071
02:22:22.343 --> 02:22:24.030
that I think that's the most powerful thing you can do

4072
02:22:24.030 --> 02:22:27.760
to make people see it as legitimate for you

4073
02:22:27.760 --> 02:22:29.480
and then also probably in the back of their minds

4074
02:22:29.480 --> 02:22:32.243
are considering should they also do it?

4075
02:22:34.070 --> 02:22:36.820
And for me, I never forget

4076
02:22:36.820 --> 02:22:38.800
why I got into this in the first place.

4077
02:22:38.800 --> 02:22:40.293
That always compels me.

4078
02:22:41.240 --> 02:22:45.350
So, I'm not going to make sacrifices

4079
02:22:45.350 --> 02:22:48.150
or fall into some sort of trap,

4080
02:22:48.150 --> 02:22:50.090
where I'm tempted to consume this or that

4081
02:22:50.090 --> 02:22:51.340
because that's the only thing available

4082
02:22:51.340 --> 02:22:54.900
and I've been flying from here to Australia for 17 hours

4083
02:22:54.900 --> 02:22:56.890
and I'm hungry or whatever the case is.

4084
02:22:56.890 --> 02:23:01.010
I just always remember why I came to a plant-based diet

4085
02:23:01.010 --> 02:23:01.960
or vegan lifestyle.

4086
02:23:01.960 --> 02:23:05.510
And that really compels me in all the actions that I do.

4087
02:23:05.510 --> 02:23:10.330
So like Matt, I also kind of laugh things off.

4088
02:23:10.330 --> 02:23:12.510
I'm not combative with people

4089
02:23:12.510 --> 02:23:14.480
because I realized that's what they're trying

4090
02:23:14.480 --> 02:23:15.380
to get out of me,

4091
02:23:15.380 --> 02:23:17.320
including places like...

4092
02:23:17.320 --> 02:23:20.130
Some of the awful places of the world are the internet.

4093
02:23:20.130 --> 02:23:21.720
Twitter is a pretty awful place.

4094
02:23:21.720 --> 02:23:24.067
YouTube comments maybe the worst place on the internet,

4095
02:23:24.067 --> 02:23:26.643
I'm not sure, but so I've heard.

4096
02:23:27.630 --> 02:23:28.530
I just woke up to...

4097
02:23:28.530 --> 02:23:29.868
Here I am, enthusiastic,

4098
02:23:29.868 --> 02:23:31.780
I'm here to do the Rich Roll Podcast,

4099
02:23:31.780 --> 02:23:32.613
I'm hanging out with Matt,

4100
02:23:32.613 --> 02:23:33.446
our book is coming out

4101
02:23:33.446 --> 02:23:36.270
and I realized that I'm in some sort of Twitter thread

4102
02:23:36.270 --> 02:23:37.807
that someone volunteered me to be part of.

4103
02:23:37.807 --> 02:23:39.270
It was like, Robert's an example

4104
02:23:39.270 --> 02:23:40.850
of how you can be big and strong

4105
02:23:40.850 --> 02:23:42.820
and they're just kind of fighting an argument,

4106
02:23:42.820 --> 02:23:44.390
but using me as their ammo.

4107
02:23:44.390 --> 02:23:47.749
And so, now all the comments are negative about me,

4108
02:23:47.749 --> 02:23:48.890
(laughs)

4109
02:23:48.890 --> 02:23:51.310
but I can't let that bother me and I don't engage them.

4110
02:23:51.310 --> 02:23:53.010
I just ignore all of that stuff.

4111
02:23:53.010 --> 02:23:54.936
And that's what I do.

4112
02:23:54.936 --> 02:23:57.370
I learned a long time ago from Dale Carnegie,

4113
02:23:57.370 --> 02:23:59.710
the best way to win an argument is to avoid one.

4114
02:23:59.710 --> 02:24:02.030
And that doesn't mean that it's taken a step back

4115
02:24:02.030 --> 02:24:03.153
for activism or anything like that.

4116
02:24:03.153 --> 02:24:04.743
It's not how I see it,

4117
02:24:05.821 --> 02:24:08.970
but I see it that the people who are trying

4118
02:24:08.970 --> 02:24:11.450
to do these deliberate acts

4119
02:24:11.450 --> 02:24:14.260
or deliberate attacks or deliberately make fun of,

4120
02:24:14.260 --> 02:24:19.130
I don't allow that to be an argument that I participate in,

4121
02:24:19.130 --> 02:24:21.670
but in a more practical sense, what you're talking about,

4122
02:24:21.670 --> 02:24:23.660
I'm actually dealing with right now.

4123
02:24:23.660 --> 02:24:27.390
My wife and I recently moved to Fort Collins, Colorado

4124
02:24:27.390 --> 02:24:28.480
about a year ago

4125
02:24:28.480 --> 02:24:30.660
and we've had this pandemic going on.

4126
02:24:30.660 --> 02:24:32.907
So, just now neighbors are starting to say,

4127
02:24:32.907 --> 02:24:35.460
"Hey, come on over for some beers and barbecue,"

4128
02:24:35.460 --> 02:24:36.293
and all this stuff

4129
02:24:36.293 --> 02:24:39.420
and I'm trying to figure out how to tell them

4130
02:24:39.420 --> 02:24:42.210
that maybe that won't work for me,

4131
02:24:42.210 --> 02:24:43.410
but we're getting a grill

4132
02:24:43.410 --> 02:24:45.277
and we have all the Beyond Burgers

4133
02:24:45.277 --> 02:24:46.300
and all that kind of stuff

4134
02:24:46.300 --> 02:24:49.080
and we're gonna kind of show them our stuff--

4135
02:24:49.080 --> 02:24:52.180
Well, you should invite them over to your house first

4136
02:24:52.180 --> 02:24:54.755
for "Hey, we're throwing a vegan barbecue,"

4137
02:24:54.755 --> 02:24:55.840
and you'll be the hit of the neighborhood.

4138
02:24:55.840 --> 02:24:57.141
Everyone will love you.

4139
02:24:57.141 --> 02:24:57.974
(laughs)

4140
02:24:57.974 --> 02:24:59.390
And what's funny is they already know about my book

4141
02:24:59.390 --> 02:25:01.300
because I can't stop talking about it, of course.

4142
02:25:01.300 --> 02:25:02.690
They all know I have this book out.

4143
02:25:02.690 --> 02:25:03.670
You've gotta check on Amazon

4144
02:25:03.670 --> 02:25:06.030
and I'm wearing vegan on my shirt

4145
02:25:06.030 --> 02:25:08.840
and like, "Yeah, come on over for a barbecue and beer."

4146
02:25:08.840 --> 02:25:10.920
They haven't made that connection yet

4147
02:25:10.920 --> 02:25:12.530
that this plant-based--

4148
02:25:12.530 --> 02:25:14.890
It's not their job to make the connection, Robert.

4149
02:25:14.890 --> 02:25:15.723
Right.

4150
02:25:15.723 --> 02:25:16.556
You can go over there

4151
02:25:16.556 --> 02:25:19.157
and when they offer you a burger you say, "No, thanks."

4152
02:25:19.157 --> 02:25:20.717
You don't have to say anything more than that.

4153
02:25:20.717 --> 02:25:23.080
You just be like, "I'm good with this," or whatever.

4154
02:25:23.080 --> 02:25:24.840
Right, it's just a new environment for me,

4155
02:25:24.840 --> 02:25:26.840
because I've always been known as kind of the vegan guy,

4156
02:25:26.840 --> 02:25:30.380
whether it's in my family circle, relatives,

4157
02:25:30.380 --> 02:25:33.230
in-laws, holidays.

4158
02:25:33.230 --> 02:25:35.740
That's been part of my identity since I was a kid.

4159
02:25:35.740 --> 02:25:37.290
I'm the vegan guy.

4160
02:25:37.290 --> 02:25:39.300
So, I've just dealt with that.

4161
02:25:39.300 --> 02:25:40.950
People knowing that,

4162
02:25:40.950 --> 02:25:45.050
but now in a new city, new neighbors, new environment,

4163
02:25:45.050 --> 02:25:47.700
I kind of have to show people, I guess,

4164
02:25:47.700 --> 02:25:48.677
who I am or--

4165
02:25:50.140 --> 02:25:52.510
I could see you're literally struggling

4166
02:25:52.510 --> 02:25:53.490
in real time with this,

4167
02:25:53.490 --> 02:25:55.300
but I think that's the relatable thing.

4168
02:25:55.300 --> 02:25:56.590
That was the reason for the question,

4169
02:25:56.590 --> 02:26:01.590
because I think people who are trying to make this switch

4170
02:26:01.770 --> 02:26:02.880
have a lot of trepidation

4171
02:26:02.880 --> 02:26:04.360
about how they're gonna deal with their neighbors

4172
02:26:04.360 --> 02:26:05.990
or their friends or their relatives.

4173
02:26:05.990 --> 02:26:07.700
You've been living this for a very long time,

4174
02:26:07.700 --> 02:26:09.370
but you've been doing it in a situation

4175
02:26:09.370 --> 02:26:12.897
in which everybody's briefed on who you are,

4176
02:26:12.897 --> 02:26:17.550
but now you're standing in the shoes of the newcomer,

4177
02:26:17.550 --> 02:26:18.630
so to speak,

4178
02:26:18.630 --> 02:26:23.630
who's trying to figure out how to be gracious and graceful

4179
02:26:23.700 --> 02:26:27.363
